{"items":[{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-10-aws-service-catalog-support-infrastructure-code-provisioning-tools","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/10/aws-service-catalog-support-infrastructure-code-provisioning-tools/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:06:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:47:20+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog customers can now create, distribute, and launch AWS resources that are configured using third- party Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools such as Ansible, Chef, Pulumi, Puppet, and more.  Within AWS Service Catalog, customers can use these IaC tools in addition to previously supported AWS CloudFormation and HashiCorp Terraform Cloud configurations.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith the launch of this feature, customers can rely on AWS Service Catalog as a single platform to organize, govern, and distribute their AWS resources without having to migrate or change their preferred IaC tooling. This feature can be used alongside other key capabilities within AWS Service Catalog including access control, tagging, versioning, maintaining least access privilege, and sharing pre-approved resources across thousands of AWS accounts to end-users. End-users, such as data scientists and machine learning engineers, can simply select and deploy resources from a catalog that is shared with them. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, customers can access and launch a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/aws-samples/service-catalog-engine-for-terraform-os\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003egeneric reference engine\u003c/a\u003e. The generic reference engine is required to provision governed resources using the IaC technology (e.g. HashiCorp Terraform, Ansible, Chef, etc.) and AWS Service Catalog. Deploying the reference engine is a one-time set up and can be executed within minutes. Additionally, the generic reference engine can be modified as needed depending on the IaC technology being used.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about using this feature, go \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/update_terraform_open_source_to_external.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. The feature is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/git-sync-supported-regions.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS commercial regions\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Service Catalog is available, including the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. For more information about Service Catalog, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog product page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/resources/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-10-20T18:17:36Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/10/aws-service-catalog-support-infrastructure-code-provisioning-tools/","postDateTime":"2023-10-20T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog announces support for additional Infrastructure as Code (IaC) provisioning tools ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog customers can now create, distribute, and launch AWS resources that are configured using third- party Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools such as Ansible, Chef, Pulumi, Puppet, and more.  Within AWS Service Catalog, customers can use these IaC tools in addition to previously supported AWS CloudFormation and HashiCorp Terraform Cloud configurations.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-08-aws-service-catalog-hashicorp-terraform-cloud","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/aws-service-catalog-hashicorp-terraform-cloud/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:52:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:54:06+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS announces AWS Service Catalog support for HashiCorp Terraform Cloud. With this launch, customers using Terraform Cloud can provide self-service provisioning with governance to their teams. AWS customers can now use Service Catalog as the single tool to organize, govern, and distribute their Terraform configurations within AWS at scale. Customers can access Service Catalog key features, including cataloging of standardized and pre-approved infrastructure-as-code templates, access control, cloud resources provisioning with least privilege access, versioning, sharing to thousands of AWS accounts, and tagging. End users such as engineers, database administrators, and data scientists simply see the list of products and versions they have access to, and can deploy them in a single action.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, use the HashiCorp-provided \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/hashicorp/aws-service-catalog-engine-for-tfc\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eTerraform Cloud reference engine\u003c/a\u003e on GitHub that conﬁgures the code and infrastructure required for the Terraform Cloud engine to work with AWS Service Catalog. This one-time setup takes just minutes. After that, you can start using Service Catalog to create and govern Terraform Cloud products, and share them with your end users across all your accounts.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis new feature is available via the AWS Service Catalog console in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Service Catalog is available, including the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions, Amazon Web Services China (Beijing) Region operated by Sinnet, and Amazon Web Services China (Ningxia) Region operated by NWCD.  To learn more, read the documentation on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/getstarted-Terraform.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog for Terraform\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-08-10T16:58:18Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/aws-service-catalog-hashicorp-terraform-cloud/","postDateTime":"2023-08-10T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog announces support for HashiCorp Terraform Cloud","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS announces AWS Service Catalog support for HashiCorp Terraform Cloud. With this launch, customers using Terraform Cloud can provide self-service provisioning with governance to their teams. AWS customers can now use Service Catalog as the single tool to organize, govern, and distribute their Terraform configurations within AWS at scale. Customers can access Service Catalog key features, including cataloging of standardized and pre-approved infrastructure-as-code templates, access control, cloud resources provisioning with least privilege access, versioning, sharing to thousands of AWS accounts, and tagging. End users such as engineers, database administrators, and data scientists simply see the list of products and versions they have access to, and can deploy them in a single action.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-08-aws-service-catalog-israel-tel-aviv-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/aws-service-catalog-israel-tel-aviv-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:52:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:56:46+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use AWS Service Catalog in the AWS Israel (Tel Aviv) Region to create, govern, and manage a catalog of Infrastructure as Code (IaC) templates that are approved for use on AWS. These IaC templates can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog helps you centrally curate and share commonly deployed templates across teams to achieve consistent governance and meet compliance requirements. End users such as engineers, database administrators, and data scientists simply see the list of products and versions they have access to, and can deploy them in a single action.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith AWS Service Catalog, organizations can control which laC templates and versions are available, what they configure in each of the available services, and who can access each template, based on individual, group, department, or cost center. Enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers use AWS Service Catalog to organize, govern, and provision resources on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog product page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/resources/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-08-07T20:41:27Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/aws-service-catalog-israel-tel-aviv-region/","postDateTime":"2023-08-07T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog is now available in the AWS Israel (Tel Aviv) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use AWS Service Catalog in the AWS Israel (Tel Aviv) Region to create, govern, and manage a catalog of Infrastructure as Code (IaC) templates that are approved for use on AWS. These IaC templates can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog helps you centrally curate and share commonly deployed templates across teams to achieve consistent governance and meet compliance requirements. End users such as engineers, database administrators, and data scientists simply see the list of products and versions they have access to, and can deploy them in a single action.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-05-aws-service-catalog-wildcards-iam-principal-name-associations","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/05/aws-service-catalog-wildcards-iam-principal-name-associations/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:01:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:45:11+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now supports granting portfolio access to IAM principal (user, group or role) names with wildcards, such as ‘*’ or ‘?’. This enables flexible and efficient sharing of infrastructure-as-code templates for customers using wildcard patterns to cover multiple IAM principal names at a time. Previously, customers had to use the exact IAM principal names to share a portfolio. Customers using AWS IAM Identity Center (successor to AWS Single Sign-On) can now quickly grant their workforce users access to Service Catalog portfolio products.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eService Catalog administrators often use portfolios in a central account to organize their Service Catalog products and then share those portfolios within their AWS Organization. With today’s launch, customers can now use “*” or “?” wildcards to associate multiple IAM principal names that match a pattern (for example, role/developer_? will match developer_1, and developer_n). After associating IAM principal names to portfolios, administrators can then share these associations along with the portfolios in their AWS Organizations using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-service-catalog-sharing-principal-names-portfolio-organization/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eOrganizational Principal Name Sharing\u003c/a\u003e. Together, these features facilitate automatic shared portfolio access to a specific group of IAM principals across thousands of accounts. Customers using AWS Identity Center can use the “role/AWSReservedSSO_{Policyname}_*” pattern to give their workforce users access to shared AWS Service Catalog products.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis new feature is available via the AWS API, AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI), and the Service Catalog console across all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where Service Catalog is available.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about wildcard principal name association, visit the\u0026nbsp;Service Catalog \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/dg/API_AssociatePrincipalWithPortfolio.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-05-31T21:18:40Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/05/aws-service-catalog-wildcards-iam-principal-name-associations/","postDateTime":"2023-05-31T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog now supports wildcards in IAM principal name associations","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now supports granting portfolio access to IAM principal (user, group or role) names with wildcards, such as ‘*’ or ‘?’. This enables flexible and efficient sharing of infrastructure-as-code templates for customers using wildcard patterns to cover multiple IAM principal names at a time. Previously, customers had to use the exact IAM principal names to share a portfolio. Customers using AWS IAM Identity Center (successor to AWS Single Sign-On) can now quickly grant their workforce users access to Service Catalog portfolio products.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-05-aws-service-management-connector-provisioning-terraform","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/05/aws-service-management-connector-provisioning-terraform/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:00:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:49:49+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use AWS Service Catalog to enable self-service provisioning of Terraform configurations in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/service-management-connector/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector\u003c/a\u003e for ServiceNow. These Terraform products will render as ServiceNow Service Catalog items that can leverage approvals and business workflows within ServiceNow. Customers can now use AWS Service Catalog as the single tool to organize, govern, and distribute their Terraform configurations within AWS at scale.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition to supporting the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/getstarted-Terraform.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog for Terraform open source\u003c/a\u003e, this launch also enables discovery of Amazon WorkSpaces, Amazon ECS, Amazon EKS, Amazon EFS in ServiceNow CMDB (Configuration Management Database) through AWS Config integration. The launch also introduces a dashboard that gives you quick access to reports/charts for AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config and AWS Security Hub integrations. The Connector also includes existing integrations with AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager, AWS Health, AWS Support, AWS Systems Manager Automation, AWS Systems Manager Change Manager. These AWS Cloud Operations integrations help simplify cloud provisioning, operations and resource management as well as streamline Service Management governance and oversight over AWS services.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eIt’s easy to get started. The AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow is available as an app (plug-in) to install at no-cost from the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://store.servicenow.com/sn_appstore_store.do#!/store/application/f0b117a3db32320093a7d7a0cf961912/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eServiceNow Store\u003c/a\u003e. Customers may incur cost for the AWS services used as well as the licensing for the IT service management (ITSM) tools. These new features are available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Support, AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config, AWS Systems Manager, AWS Health and AWS Security Hub services are available. For more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/integrations-servicenow.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-05-11T16:59:44Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/05/aws-service-management-connector-provisioning-terraform/","postDateTime":"2023-05-11T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Management Connector now supports provisioning with Terraform","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use AWS Service Catalog to enable self-service provisioning of Terraform configurations in the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/service-management-connector.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector\u003c/a\u003e for ServiceNow. These Terraform products will render as ServiceNow Service Catalog items that can leverage approvals and business workflows within ServiceNow. Customers can now use AWS Service Catalog as the single tool to organize, govern, and distribute their Terraform configurations within AWS at scale.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-config","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-config","description":"general:products/aws-config","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-04-aws-service-catalog-terraform-open-source","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/04/aws-service-catalog-terraform-open-source/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:44:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:02:33+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS announces AWS Service Catalog support for Terraform open source. With this launch, customers using Terraform open source can provide self-service provisioning with governance to their teams. Customers can now use Service Catalog as the single tool to organize, govern, and distribute their Terraform configurations within AWS at scale. You can access Service Catalog key features, including cataloging of standardized and pre-approved infrastructure-as-code templates, access control, cloud resources provisioning with least privilege access, versioning, sharing to thousands of AWS accounts, and tagging. End users such as engineers, database administrators, and data scientists simply see the list of products and versions they have access to, and can deploy them in a single action.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, use the AWS-provided \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/aws-samples/service-catalog-engine-for-terraform-os\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eTerraform Reference Engine on GitHub\u003c/a\u003e that conﬁgures the code and infrastructure required for the Terraform open source engine to work with AWS Service Catalog. This one-time setup takes just minutes. After that, you can start using Service Catalog to create and govern Terraform open source products, and share them with your end users across all your accounts.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis new feature is available via the\u0026nbsp;AWS Service Catalog console in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Service Catalog is available, including AWS GovCloud (US) and\u0026nbsp;China (Beijing, operated by Sinnet), and China (Ningxia, operated by NWCD).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, read the documentation on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/getstarted-Terraform.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog for Terraform open source\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-04-03T23:48:22Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/04/aws-service-catalog-terraform-open-source/","postDateTime":"2023-04-03T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog announces support for Terraform open source","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS announces AWS Service Catalog support for Terraform open source. With this launch, customers using Terraform open source can provide self-service provisioning with governance to their teams. Customers can now use Service Catalog as the single tool to organize, govern, and distribute their Terraform configurations within AWS at scale. You can access Service Catalog key features, including cataloging of standardized and pre-approved infrastructure-as-code templates, access control, cloud resources provisioning with least privilege access, versioning, sharing to thousands of AWS accounts, and tagging. End users such as engineers, database administrators, and data scientists simply see the list of products and versions they have access to, and can deploy them in a single action.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-03-aws-service-catalog-four-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/aws-service-catalog-four-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:01:21+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:45:54+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is now available to customers in four additional AWS Regions: Europe (Zurich), Europe (Spain), Asia Pacific (Hyderabad) and Asia Pacific (Melbourne).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog enables customers to create, govern, and manage a catalog of Infrastructure as Code (IaC) templates that are approved for use on AWS. These IaC templates can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog helps you centrally curate and share commonly deployed templates across teams to achieve consistent governance and meet compliance requirements.  End-users such as engineers, database administrators, and data scientists can then quickly discover and self-service approved AWS resources that they need to use to perform their daily job functions.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith AWS Service Catalog, organizations can control which laC templates and versions are available, what is configured in each of the available services, and who can access each template, based on individual, group, department, or cost center. AWS Service Catalog is used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision resources on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the AWS \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eService Catalog product page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/resources/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-03-29T21:24:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/aws-service-catalog-four-regions/","postDateTime":"2023-03-29T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog is now available in four additional AWS Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is now available to customers in four additional AWS Regions: Europe (Zurich), Europe (Spain), Asia Pacific (Hyderabad) and Asia Pacific (Melbourne).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-03-aws-service-catalog-aws-middle-east-uae-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/aws-service-catalog-aws-middle-east-uae-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:58:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:53:00+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday we are excited to announce the availability of AWS Service Catalog in the AWS Middle East (UAE) Region. AWS Service Catalog enables customers to create, govern, and manage a catalog of Infrastructure as Code (IaC) templates that are approved for use on AWS. These IaC templates can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. Service Catalog helps you centrally curate and share commonly deployed templates across teams to achieve consistent governance and meet compliance requirements.  End-users such as engineers, database administrators, and data scientists can then quickly discover and self-service approved AWS resources that they need to use to perform their daily job functions.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Service Catalog, organizations can control which laC templates and versions are available, what is configured in each of the available services, and who can access each template, based on individual, group, department, or cost center. Service Catalog is used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision resources on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eService Catalog product page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/resources/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-03-23T19:15:39Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/aws-service-catalog-aws-middle-east-uae-region/","postDateTime":"2023-03-23T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog now available in AWS Middle East (UAE) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday we are excited to announce the availability of AWS Service Catalog in the AWS Middle East (UAE) Region. AWS Service Catalog enables customers to create, govern, and manage a catalog of Infrastructure as Code (IaC) templates that are approved for use on AWS. These IaC templates can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. Service Catalog helps you centrally curate and share commonly deployed templates across teams to achieve consistent governance and meet compliance requirements.  End-users such as engineers, database administrators, and data scientists can then quickly discover and self-service approved AWS resources that they need to use to perform their daily job functions.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-02-aws-service-catalog-disassociate-delete-products-one-action","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/02/aws-service-catalog-disassociate-delete-products-one-action/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:55:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:29:54+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog customers can now disassociate and delete their AWS Service Catalog products in one-action, making it easier to update and manage their catalog of AWS resources. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers use AWS Service Catalog to manage and share their infrastructure-as-code templates, and apply governance to them. These templates are saved as products in AWS Service Catalog, and can be arranged in logical sets called portfolios. Prior to this feature, customers were prevented from deleting products if there were any associated resource components. For example, customers would have to manually and individually disassociate other resource components such as portfolio associations, TagOptions, Service Actions, and Budgets, prior to being able to delete their AWS Service Catalog products. Now, using the console or creating a custom alias through the AWS Command Line Interface (CLI), customers can efficiently delete their AWS products in one step. When customers select ‘Delete’ from the console, a new module will appear that lists all the components that are associated for a given AWS Service Catalog product. Customers can see and verify these associations and upon confirmation, select ‘Disassociate and Delete’, which will automatically disassociate all components and delete the AWS product.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about using this feature, go \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/productmgmt-delete.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. The feature is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Service Catalog is available. For more information about Service Catalog, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog product page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/resources/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-02-27T22:28:50Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/02/aws-service-catalog-disassociate-delete-products-one-action/","postDateTime":"2023-02-27T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog now supports the ability to disassociate and delete products in one-action","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog customers can now disassociate and delete their AWS Service Catalog products in one-action, making it easier to update and manage their catalog of AWS resources. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-02-aws-service-management-connector-jira-service-management-customer-portal","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/02/aws-service-management-connector-jira-service-management-customer-portal/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:57:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:39:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can search, provision, terminate, update and use self-service actions on products from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e through Atlassian’s Jira Service Management Cloud customer portal via \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/service-management-connector/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector\u003c/a\u003e. This feature enables Jira Service Management end users who are registered users of the Atlassian site but are not Jira agents to provision resources using the AWS Service Catalog integration. With this connector, administrators can use existing AWS Service Catalog configurations, including curated products, portfolios, constraints, and tagging, and expose them to Jira Service Management Cloud administrators and users. Jira Service Management customers can browse and request provisioning of AWS Service Catalog products in their familiar IT Service Management (ITSM) tooling.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition to the AWS Service Catalog integration, the connector also provides existing integrations with AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager and AWS Security Hub. These AWS CloudOps integrations help simplify cloud provisioning, operations and resource management as well as streamline Service Management governance and oversight over AWS services.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Service Management Connector are available as plugins/apps to install at no-cost from the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/1221283/aws-service-management-connector-for-jsm?tab\u003doverview\u0026amp;hosting\u003dcloud\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAtlassian Marketplace\u003c/a\u003e. Customers may incur cost for the AWS services used as well as the licensing for the ITSM tools. These new features are available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Service Catalog, AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager and AWS Security Hub services are available. For more information, please visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/smc/latest/ag/integrations-jsmcloud.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-02-07T18:03:35Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/02/aws-service-management-connector-jira-service-management-customer-portal/","postDateTime":"2023-02-07T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Management Connector for Jira Service Management customer portal","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can search, provision, terminate, update and use self-service actions on products from \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/servicecatalog.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e through Atlassian’s Jira Service Management Cloud customer portal via \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/service-management-connector.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector\u003c/a\u003e. This feature enables Jira Service Management end users who are registered users of the Atlassian site but are not Jira agents to provision resources using the AWS Service Catalog integration. With this connector, administrators can use existing AWS Service Catalog configurations, including curated products, portfolios, constraints, and tagging, and expose them to Jira Service Management Cloud administrators and users. Jira Service Management customers can browse and request provisioning of AWS Service Catalog products in their familiar IT Service Management (ITSM) tooling.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-aws-control-tower-account-customization","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-control-tower-account-customization/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:46:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:20:45+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Control Tower now offers support for account factory customization, enabling you to customize your new and existing AWS accounts prior to provisioning them from within the AWS Control Tower console. With this release, you can now use AWS Control Tower to define account blueprints that scale your multi-account provisioning without starting from scratch with every account. An account blueprint describes the specific resources and configurations that are used when an account is provisioned. You may also use pre-defined blueprints, built and managed by AWS partners, to customize accounts for specific use cases.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers often need to customize their accounts to meet their business needs. Previously, customers used AWS Control Tower’s pre-defined account blueprint, with default resources, configurations, and VPC, or developed alternative solutions to add customizations to their accounts. In AWS Control Tower, you can now define and implement custom account requirements as part of a well-defined account factory workflow, and immediately start using the account after it is provisioned. AWS Control Tower automates the entire process on your behalf, freeing you from the need to build and maintain costly deployment pipelines.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Control Tower offers a streamlined way to set up and govern a new, secure, multi-account AWS environment based on AWS best practices. You can start customizing accounts now in AWS Control Tower. To learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/controltower/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Control Tower homepage\u003c/a\u003e or see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/af-customization-page.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Control Tower User Guide\u003c/a\u003e. Account factory customization is generally available in the following AWS Regions: US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), Canada (Central) Region, Asia, Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Singapore) Region, Europe (Frankfurt) Region, Europe (Ireland), Europe (London) Region, Europe (Stockholm) Region, Asia Pacific (Mumbai) Region, Asia Pacific (Seoul) Region , Asia Pacific (Tokyo) Region, Europe (Paris) Region, South America (São Paulo) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn how to create these customizations, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/productmgmt-cloudresource.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation on creating products in AWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e. You can also select partner-managed blueprints from the Getting Started Library in Service Catalog, which includes solutions from CSS, Datadog, F5, Fortinet, Snyk, Splunk, Sysdig, Cisco, Cribl, Effectual and Lacework.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-28T18:47:21Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-control-tower-account-customization/","postDateTime":"2022-11-28T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing account customization within AWS Control Tower","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Control Tower now offers support for account factory customization, enabling you to customize your new and existing AWS accounts prior to provisioning them from within the AWS Control Tower console. With this release, you can now use AWS Control Tower to define account blueprints that scale your multi-account provisioning without starting from scratch with every account. An account blueprint describes the specific resources and configurations that are used when an account is provisioned. You may also use pre-defined blueprints, built and managed by AWS partners, to customize accounts for specific use cases.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-control-tower","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-control-tower","description":"general:products/aws-control-tower","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-service-catalog-syncing-products-infrastructure-code-template-files-github-enterprise-bitbucket","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/service-catalog-syncing-products-infrastructure-code-template-files-github-enterprise-bitbucket/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:41:26+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:51:18+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog customers can now create AWS Service Catalog products that are synced to Infrastructure as Code (IaC) templates that are managed in external repositories such as GitHub, GitHub Enterprise, or Bitbucket.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog customers often manage their IaC templates in an external repository, such as GitHub, GitHub Enterprise or BitBucket. When creating new or updating existing product versions, they have to build and manage separate code pipelines that ensure alignment between their AWS Service Catalog product versions and the template files in their repositories. With today’s launch, AWS Service Catalog customers no longer need to build and manage this additional code infrastructure. They can use their external repositories as a single source of truth to manage and update their IaC template files, and AWS Service Catalog will sync changes automatically.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo create synced AWS Service Catalog products, customers must authorize a one-time connection between their AWS account and external third-party provider account using AWS CodeStar Connections. Once a connection is established, AWS Service Catalog administrators can create new or update existing AWS Service Catalog products based on a template file within a given repository and branch. If a change to the template file is committed in the repository, AWS Service Catalog will automatically detect the change and create a new product version. Previous product versions will be maintained up to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/limits.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eprescribed version limit\u003c/a\u003e and their status is changed to ‘deprecated’. This feature for AWS Service Catalog can be used through the AWS Command Line Interface(CLI), AWS API, or through the AWS Service Catalog console.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about using GitHub, GitHub Enterprise or BitBucket with AWS Service Catalog, go \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/git-synced-sc-products.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. The feature is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https//docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/git-sync-supported-regions.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS commercial regions\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Service Catalog and AWS CodeStar Connection are available. For more information about Service Catalog, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog product page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/resources/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-21T21:23:32Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/service-catalog-syncing-products-infrastructure-code-template-files-github-enterprise-bitbucket/","postDateTime":"2022-11-21T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog now supports syncing products with Infrastructure as Code template files from GitHub, GitHub Enterprise, or Bitbucket ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog customers can now create AWS Service Catalog products that are synced to Infrastructure as Code (IaC) templates that are managed in external repositories such as GitHub, GitHub Enterprise, or Bitbucket.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-aws-service-catalog-sharing-principal-names-portfolio-organization","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-service-catalog-sharing-principal-names-portfolio-organization/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:56:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:49:28+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now supports the sharing of principal names when sharing a portfolio, which simplifies the workflow for granting access to portfolios shared across multiple accounts in an AWS Organization. Administrators often use portfolios in a central account to regroup and organize their AWS Service Catalog products and then share those portfolios with different accounts in their AWS Organization. Previously, to grant end users access to a shared portfolio, administrators had to associate IAM principals (groups, roles or users) with the portfolio in each recipient account.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith this new feature, AWS Service Catalog administrators can define principal names, which are names for IAM groups, roles and users, and associate them with a portfolio. When sharing a portfolio within an AWS Organization, administrators can now share these principal names along with the portfolio with all accounts in the Organization, within an Organizational Unit (OU) or with specific Organization member accounts. In each recipient account, AWS Service Catalog verifies if IAM principals with those names exists, and if they do, AWS Service Catalog automatically grants the matching IAM principals access to the shared portfolio. When administrators add or remove principal names from the shared portfolio, AWS Service Catalog automatically applies those changes in the recipient accounts.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith today’s launch, AWS Service Catalog administrators can centrally manage and control access to their shared portfolios and no longer need to associate IAM principals with portfolios in each recipient account. This new feature is available via the AWS API, AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI), and the AWS Service Catalog console in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS commercial\u0026nbsp;Regions\u003c/a\u003e expect China Regions and AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. To learn more about how to share principal names when sharing a portfolio within an AWS Organization, visit the AWS Service Catalog \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/catalogs_portfolios_sharing_how-to-share.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAdministrator Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-18T23:28:31Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-service-catalog-sharing-principal-names-portfolio-organization/","postDateTime":"2022-11-18T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog now supports the sharing of principal names when sharing a portfolio within an AWS Organization","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now supports the sharing of principal names when sharing a portfolio, which simplifies the workflow for granting access to portfolios shared across multiple accounts in an AWS Organization. Administrators often use portfolios in a central account to regroup and organize their AWS Service Catalog products and then share those portfolios with different accounts in their AWS Organization. Previously, to grant end users access to a shared portfolio, administrators had to associate IAM principals (groups, roles or users) with the portfolio in each recipient account.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-service-catalog-appregistry-support-automatic-associations-based-tags","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/service-catalog-appregistry-support-automatic-associations-based-tags/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:45:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:01:14+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Service Catalog announces support for automatic association of application resources in AppRegistry based on AWS tags. With this release, customers can build applications using their preferred tools, and the associated resources are automatically added to the application based on their tags. Once registered, AppRegistry applications and their resources can be managed and assessed in tools like AWS Systems Manager Application Manager, AWS CloudWatch Application Insights, AWS Well-Architected, and AWS Resilience Hub.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eYou can now define the application tag key and value in AppRegistry, and resources are automatically added to your application as they are created. AppRegistry creates the application and an AWS Resource Group to track and help you structure and manage your application resources. From Application Manager, you can view the resources that power your application, as well as application cost using AWS Cost Explorer, Amazon CloudWatch alarms, AWS Config rule compliance, and Systems Manager OpsItems. AWS Systems Manager Automation Runbooks are also available to take action on your application’s resources.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is available via the AWS Console, API and AWS Command Line Interface (CLI) in all AWS Regions except the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions, Amazon Web Services China (Beijing) region, operated by Sinnet, and the Amazon Web Services China (Ningxia) region, operated by NWCD. To learn more, read\u0026nbsp;the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/arguide/intro-app-registry.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation on the Service Catalog AppRegistry\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-18T21:17:43Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/service-catalog-appregistry-support-automatic-associations-based-tags/","postDateTime":"2022-11-18T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing AWS Service Catalog AppRegistry support for automatic associations based on tags ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Service Catalog announces support for automatic association of application resources in AppRegistry based on AWS tags. With this release, customers can build applications using their preferred tools, and the associated resources are automatically added to the application based on their tags. Once registered, AppRegistry applications and their resources can be managed and assessed in tools like AWS Systems Manager Application Manager, AWS CloudWatch Application Insights, AWS Well-Architected, and AWS Resilience Hub.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-systems-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-systems-manager","description":"general:products/aws-systems-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-aws-systems-manager-responses-jira-cloud-service-management-connector","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-systems-manager-responses-jira-cloud-service-management-connector/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:55:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:50:32+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can respond, investigate and resolve incidents affecting their AWS-hosted applications via \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/features/incident-manager/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Systems Manager Incident Manager\u003c/a\u003e with the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/service-management-connector/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector\u003c/a\u003e. This integration is built using Atlassian Forge for Atlassian\u0027s Jira Service Management (JSM) Cloud. AWS Systems Manager is the operations hub for AWS applications and resources, that helps to automate reactive processes to quickly diagnose and remediate operational issues. With the Incident Manager integration with JSM Cloud, customers can now automate their incident response plans in Incident Manager and automatically synchronize their incidents into JSM Cloud. This feature enables faster resolution of critical application availability and performance issues without disrupting existing workflows in Jira Service Management Cloud.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition to the AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager integration, this release also introduces integrations of AWS Service Catalog to request and provision products, and AWS Security Hub for bidirectional synchronization of AWS Security Hub findings. These AWS CloudOps integrations help simplify cloud provisioning, operations and resource management as well as streamline Service Management governance and oversight over AWS services.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Management Connector for Jira Service Management Cloud plugin is available at no charge in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/1221283/aws-service-management-connector-for-jsm?tab\u003doverview\u0026amp;hosting\u003dcloud\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAtlassian Marketplace\u003c/a\u003e. These new features are available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Service Catalog, AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager and AWS Security Hub services are available. For more information, please visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/smc/latest/ag/integrations-jsmcloud.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-17T18:02:48Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-systems-manager-responses-jira-cloud-service-management-connector/","postDateTime":"2022-11-17T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager now streamlines responses to Jira Service Management Cloud Incidents via AWS Service Management Connector","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can respond, investigate and resolve incidents affecting their AWS-hosted applications via \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/systems-manager/features/incident-manager.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Systems Manager Incident Manager\u003c/a\u003e with the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/service-management-connector.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector\u003c/a\u003e. This integration is built using Atlassian Forge for Atlassian\u0027s Jira Service Management (JSM) Cloud. AWS Systems Manager is the operations hub for AWS applications and resources, that helps to automate reactive processes to quickly diagnose and remediate operational issues. With the Incident Manager integration with JSM Cloud, customers can now automate their incident response plans in Incident Manager and automatically synchronize their incidents into JSM Cloud. This feature enables faster resolution of critical application availability and performance issues without disrupting existing workflows in Jira Service Management Cloud.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-security-hub","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-security-hub","description":"general:products/aws-security-hub","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:36+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-systems-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-systems-manager","description":"general:products/aws-systems-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-aws-security-hub-bidirectional-integration-connector-atlassians-jira-management-cloud","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-security-hub-bidirectional-integration-connector-atlassians-jira-management-cloud/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:53:38+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:34:28+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStaring today, customers can detect and resolve AWS security findings from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/security-hub/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Security Hub\u003c/a\u003e via \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/service-management-connector/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector\u003c/a\u003e. This integration is built using Atlassian Forge for Atlassian\u0027s Jira Service Management (JSM) Cloud. AWS Security Hub helps customers to perform security best practice checks, aggregate alerts and enables automated remediation. It enables users to view security findings from AWS services, such as Amazon Guard Duty, Amazon Inspector, as well as AWS Partner solutions. This bidirectional integration between AWS Security Hub and Jira Service Management incidents enables JSM users/developers to manage AWS Security findings while leveraging their existing workflows in Jira Service Management (incidents).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition to the AWS Security Hub integration, this release also introduces integrations with AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager incident creation and management, and provisioning of AWS resources via AWS Service Catalog. These AWS CloudOps integrations help simplify cloud provisioning, operations and resource management as well as streamline Service Management governance and oversight over AWS services.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Management Connector for Jira Service Management Cloud plugin is available at no charge in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/1221283/aws-service-management-connector-for-jsm?tab\u003doverview\u0026amp;hosting\u003dcloud\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAtlassian Marketplace\u003c/a\u003e. These new features are available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Service Catalog, AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager and AWS Security Hub services are available. For more information, please visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/smc/latest/ag/integrations-jsmcloud.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-17T18:22:30Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-security-hub-bidirectional-integration-connector-atlassians-jira-management-cloud/","postDateTime":"2022-11-17T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":" AWS Security Hub now supports bidirectional integration via AWS Service Management Connector for Atlassian’s Jira Service Management Cloud","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStaring today, customers can detect and resolve AWS security findings from \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/security-hub.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Security Hub\u003c/a\u003e via \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/service-management-connector.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector\u003c/a\u003e. This integration is built using Atlassian Forge for Atlassian\u0027s Jira Service Management (JSM) Cloud. AWS Security Hub helps customers to perform security best practice checks, aggregate alerts and enables automated remediation. It enables users to view security findings from AWS services, such as Amazon Guard Duty, Amazon Inspector, as well as AWS Partner solutions. This bidirectional integration between AWS Security Hub and Jira Service Management incidents enables JSM users/developers to manage AWS Security findings while leveraging their existing workflows in Jira Service Management (incidents).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-systems-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-systems-manager","description":"general:products/aws-systems-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#security-identity-and-compliance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"security-identity-and-compliance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/security-identity-and-compliance","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-security-hub","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-security-hub","description":"general:products/aws-security-hub","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:36+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-aws-service-management-connector-catalog-jira-service-management-cloud","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-service-management-connector-catalog-jira-service-management-cloud/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:54:26+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:47:55+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can search, request and provision products from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e via \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/service-management-connector/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector\u003c/a\u003e. This integration is built using Atlassian Forge for Atlassian\u0027s Jira Service Management (JSM) Cloud. With this connector, administrators can use existing AWS Service Catalog configurations, including curated products, portfolios, constraints, and tagging, and expose them to JSM Cloud administrators and users. Administrators can view AWS Service Catalog portfolios and products, align them to organizational structures, grant access to JSM Cloud users, and connect JSM workflows to provisioning requests. JSM Cloud end users can browse and request provisioning of AWS Service Catalog products, including AWS Marketplace software products that have been copied to AWS Service Catalog.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition to the AWS Service Catalog integration, this release also introduces integrations of AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager incident creation and management, and AWS Security Hub for bidirectional synchronization of AWS Security Hub findings. These AWS CloudOps integrations help simplify cloud provisioning, operations and resource management as well as streamline Service Management governance and oversight over AWS services.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Management Connector for Jira Service Management Cloud plugin is available at no charge in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/1221283/aws-service-management-connector-for-jsm?tab\u003doverview\u0026amp;hosting\u003dcloud\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAtlassian Marketplace\u003c/a\u003e. These new features are available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Service Catalog, AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager and AWS Security Hub services are available. For more information, please visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/smc/latest/ag/integrations-jsmcloud.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-17T18:18:20Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-service-management-connector-catalog-jira-service-management-cloud/","postDateTime":"2022-11-17T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Management Connector now supports provisioning AWS Service Catalog products in Atlassian’s Jira Service Management Cloud","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can search, request and provision products from \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/servicecatalog.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e via \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/service-management-connector.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector\u003c/a\u003e. This integration is built using Atlassian Forge for Atlassian\u0027s Jira Service Management (JSM) Cloud. With this connector, administrators can use existing AWS Service Catalog configurations, including curated products, portfolios, constraints, and tagging, and expose them to JSM Cloud administrators and users. Administrators can view AWS Service Catalog portfolios and products, align them to organizational structures, grant access to JSM Cloud users, and connect JSM workflows to provisioning requests. JSM Cloud end users can browse and request provisioning of AWS Service Catalog products, including AWS Marketplace software products that have been copied to AWS Service Catalog.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-systems-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-systems-manager","description":"general:products/aws-systems-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-security-hub","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-security-hub","description":"general:products/aws-security-hub","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:36+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-aws-well-architected-tool-workload-discovery-speeds-reviews","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-well-architected-tool-workload-discovery-speeds-reviews/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:53:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:24:10+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS is pleased to announce the availability of two new features in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/well-architected-tool/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Well-Architected Tool\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;(AWS WA Tool)—integrations with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/premiumsupport/technology/trusted-advisor/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Trusted Advisor\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/arguide/intro-app-registry.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog AppRegistry\u003c/a\u003e—that will help you more easily discover the information needed to answer Well-Architected review questions and shorten your review time. \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003ePreviously, customers conducting AWS Well-Architected Framework reviews had to spend time verifying their answers by double checking their workloads to see if they were following best practices; there wasn’t a clear link between the workload being reviewed and it’s associated resources. With the AWS Trusted Advisor integration, the AWS WA Tool now presents findings based on automated Trusted Advisor resource checks, providing you with further contextual information during your reviews. This change improves the accuracy of your answers and the speed of your review. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS WA Tool is also now integrated with AWS Service Catalog AppRegistry. AWS Service Catalog AppRegistry lets you store your AWS applications, their associated resource collections, and application attribute groups. The integration with AWS Service Catalog AppRegistry provides you with better visibility into which applications are associated with which workloads during the Well-Architected review process, saving you time by tracking and organizing your workload\u0027s associated resources.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog AppRegistry in the AWS WA Tool is generally available for all customers. Access to AWS Trusted Advisor checks within the AWS WA Tool is based on the customer\u0027s AWS Support Plan. The AWS WA Tool is available in the following AWS Regions: US East (N. Virginia, Ohio), US West (N. California, Oregon), Canada (Central), Europe (Frankfurt, Ireland, London, Paris, Stockholm), South America (Sao Paulo), Asia Pacific (Singapore, Sydney, Tokyo, Seoul, Mumbai, Hong Kong), Middle East (Bahrain), and AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started with the new AWS Trusted Advisor integration, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS WA Tool in the AWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and turn on AWS Trusted Advisor support or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/userguide/intro.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eview documentation\u003c/a\u003e. To get started with the new AWS Service Catalog AppRegistry integration, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS WA Tool in the AWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and add resources to a new or existing workload.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-07T20:46:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-well-architected-tool-workload-discovery-speeds-reviews/","postDateTime":"2022-11-07T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Well-Architected Tool improves workload discovery and speeds up reviews","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS is pleased to announce the availability of two new features in the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/well-architected-tool.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Well-Architected Tool\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;(AWS WA Tool)—integrations with \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/premiumsupport/technology/trusted-advisor.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Trusted Advisor\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/arguide/intro-app-registry.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog AppRegistry\u003c/a\u003e—that will help you more easily discover the information needed to answer Well-Architected review questions and shorten your review time. \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-well-architected-tool","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-well-architected-tool","description":"general:products/aws-well-architected-tool","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:31+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-trusted-advisor","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-trusted-advisor","description":"general:products/aws-trusted-advisor","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:58:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:58:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-10-aws-service-management-connector-streamlines-display-aws-service-catalog-products-account-region-servicenow-service-portal","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/10/aws-service-management-connector-streamlines-display-aws-service-catalog-products-account-region-servicenow-service-portal/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:43:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:00:49+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/service-management-connector/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector\u003c/a\u003e for\u0026nbsp;ServiceNow (version 4.7.5) enables customers to streamline the display of AWS Service Catalog portfolios and products by Account and Region in ServiceNow Service Portal. This feature enables ServiceNow Service Portal end users to identify and drill-down to the appropriate AWS Service Catalog product if they have access to shared portfolios from multiple accounts and regions. Previously the drilldown feature was restricted to only portfolio names. This version also includes additional filter navigator modules for open incidents in AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager integration and displays timeline events as comments on the AWS incident in user-readable format. The AWS Support integration now introduces an optional configuration to create the support cases in an intermediate table for customers who want to leverage custom business workflows for managing support cases. The AWS Service Management Connector supports latest ServiceNow releases for Tokyo(T), San Diego(S) and Rome (R).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers can use the AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow to provision AWS resources and manage operations and incident response for AWS resources. ServiceNow administrators can configure the connector to work with new or existing AWS accounts, and associate one or more AWS accounts to ServiceNow. The connector also provides integrations with AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config, AWS Health Dashboard, AWS Systems Manager OpsCenter, AWS Systems Manager Automation, AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager, AWS Change Manager Systems Manager, AWS Support and AWS Security Hub, which helps simplify cloud provisioning, operations and resource management as well as streamline Service Management governance and oversight over AWS services.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eIt’s easy to get started. The AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow is available at no charge in\u0026nbsp;the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://store.servicenow.com/sn_appstore_store.do#!/store/application/f0b117a3db32320093a7d7a0cf961912/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eServiceNow Store\u003c/a\u003e. These new features are generally available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Support, AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config, AWS Systems Manager, AWS Health Dashboard, AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager and AWS Security Hub services are available. For more information, please visit the documentation on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/smc/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-10-20T20:13:58Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/10/aws-service-management-connector-streamlines-display-aws-service-catalog-products-account-region-servicenow-service-portal/","postDateTime":"2022-10-20T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Management Connector now streamlines display of AWS Service Catalog products by Account and Region in ServiceNow Service Portal","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/service-management-connector.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector\u003c/a\u003e for\u0026nbsp;ServiceNow (version 4.7.5) enables customers to streamline the display of AWS Service Catalog portfolios and products by Account and Region in ServiceNow Service Portal. This feature enables ServiceNow Service Portal end users to identify and drill-down to the appropriate AWS Service Catalog product if they have access to shared portfolios from multiple accounts and regions. Previously the drilldown feature was restricted to only portfolio names. This version also includes additional filter navigator modules for open incidents in AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager integration and displays timeline events as comments on the AWS incident in user-readable format. The AWS Support integration now introduces an optional configuration to create the support cases in an intermediate table for customers who want to leverage custom business workflows for managing support cases. The AWS Service Management Connector supports latest ServiceNow releases for Tokyo(T), San Diego(S) and Rome (R).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-09-aws-service-catalog-improvements-usability","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/aws-service-catalog-improvements-usability/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:53:05+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:42:23+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e AWS Service Catalog makes improvements on usability for customers who are provisioning AWS resources via the AWS Service Catalog console. These changes will help enable better error handling and reduce friction in the provisioning workflow.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith the improvements on error handling, customers will be able to debug provision errors and take actions on them more easily. Instead of seeing errors in raw JSON format, you can now see them in a more readable tabular format. This allows you to look for the most relevant errors and root cause issues more quickly. From there, you can either copy the error messages to clipboard or directly address them in CloudFormation. This reduces the effort to work across AWS consoles to one single click. The new ability to force terminate provisioned products that are in a tainted state also allows you to delete the provisioned products and disconnect it from the underlying CloudFormation stacks. Previously this was only possible through API.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith the improvements on the provisioning workflow, you can now save time and clicks when provisioning new products. Using the new autofill suggestion saves the effort to either memorize the parameters previously used to provision the same product, or going back and forth to look for the right parameters. Seeing constraint description inline with the input field will also help you provision products more quickly with less friction.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog homepage\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;or see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog Documentation\u003c/a\u003e. These new improvements are available via the Service Catalog console in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ecommercial AWS Regions and AWS GovCloud (US)\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-09-30T18:07:17Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/aws-service-catalog-improvements-usability/","postDateTime":"2022-09-30T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":" AWS Service Catalog console makes improvements on usability","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e AWS Service Catalog makes improvements on usability for customers who are provisioning AWS resources via the AWS Service Catalog console. These changes will help enable better error handling and reduce friction in the provisioning workflow.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-06-aws-service-catalogs-application-registry-cross-account-applications","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/06/aws-service-catalogs-application-registry-cross-account-applications/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:52:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:37:17+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Service Catalog announces support for cross-account AppRegistry applications and attribute groups.  With this release, applications can now be shared within your AWS Organization enabling recipient accounts to associate their local resources to shared applications. If you have application resources deployed in more than one account within your AWS Organization, you can now maintain a single repository of your applications and application metadata.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eYou first enable \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/ram/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Resource Access Manager\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;(RAM) for your AWS Organization, a service that enables customers to easily and securely share AWS resources across accounts in an Organization. Once enabled, you use RAM to share your application to your Organization, organizational unit (OU), and accounts. In order to manage your application resources, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/features/#AWS_Service_Catalog_AppRegistry_features\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAppRegistry\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;creates and maintains an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ARG/latest/userguide/resource-groups.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Resource Group\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;in every account where the shared application has resources. In these accounts you can navigate from AppRegistry to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/features/#Application_Manager\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Systems Manager Application Manager\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;to view your application resources, monitor the application operational and compliance status, view operational items, and perform runbooks against application stacks or individual resources.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAppRegistry is available via the AWS Console, API and CLI in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS commercial Regions\u003c/a\u003e. This feature is available at no additional cost. To learn more, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/dg/API_Operations_AWS_Service_Catalog_App_Registry.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation on the Service Catalog AppRegistry\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-06-16T18:13:16Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/06/aws-service-catalogs-application-registry-cross-account-applications/","postDateTime":"2022-06-16T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog\u0027s Application Registry now supports cross-account applications.","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Service Catalog announces support for cross-account AppRegistry applications and attribute groups.  With this release, applications can now be shared within your AWS Organization enabling recipient accounts to associate their local resources to shared applications. If you have application resources deployed in more than one account within your AWS Organization, you can now maintain a single repository of your applications and application metadata.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-06-aws-service-catalog-support-abac","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/06/aws-service-catalog-support-abac/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:53:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:58:03+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Web Services (AWS) Service Catalog now supports Attributed Based Access Controls (ABAC), allowing customers the ability to use tags to easily manage access and permissions to AWS resources in Service Catalog. Now, Service Catalog administrators have the ability to define their AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) policies to grant access and specify finer-grained permissions based on tags shared between AWS resource(s) and IAM users or roles. For example, based on a matching set of tags, an IAM entity (e.g., user or role) may be allowed or denied to create resources in their Service Catalog account.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eABAC is helpful to enterprises and organizations that are growing rapidly and helps with situations where policy management becomes cumbersome. With an ABAC policy in place, Service Catalog customers can set granular level of permission controls for certain users to help alleviate the administrative burden of managing all resources in a multi-account environment. These policies scale with innovation by supporting the enterprise as the number of users, accounts, and resources grow. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog’s support for ABAC is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS commercial and GovCloud Regions\u003c/a\u003e. For more information about Service Catalog, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eService Catalog product page\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/resources/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about ABAC on AWS, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/identity/attribute-based-access-control/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eABAC informational page\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/introduction_attribute-based-access-control.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-06-13T22:05:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/06/aws-service-catalog-support-abac/","postDateTime":"2022-06-13T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog announces support for Attribute Based Access Control (ABAC)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Web Services (AWS) Service Catalog now supports Attributed Based Access Controls (ABAC), allowing customers the ability to use tags to easily manage access and permissions to AWS resources in Service Catalog. Now, Service Catalog administrators have the ability to define their AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) policies to grant access and specify finer-grained permissions based on tags shared between AWS resource(s) and IAM users or roles. For example, based on a matching set of tags, an IAM entity (e.g., user or role) may be allowed or denied to create resources in their Service Catalog account.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-06-aws-service-catalog-now-available-jakarta-indonesia","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/06/aws-service-catalog-now-available-jakarta-indonesia/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:19:35+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is now available to customers in the AWS Region in (Jakarta) Indonesia.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog enables organizations on AWS to create, govern, and manage a catalog of\u0026nbsp;Infrastructure as Code (IaC) templates that are approved for use on AWS. These\u0026nbsp;IaC templates can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog administrators can centrally curate and share commonly deployed templates with their teams to achieve consistent governance and meet compliance requirements. End-users such as DevOps engineers and data scientists can then quickly discover and self-service approved AWS resources that they need to use to perform their daily job functions.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith AWS Service Catalog, organizations are able to control which laC templates and versions are available, what is configured in each of the available services, and who gets permissions access by individual, group, department, or cost center. AWS Service Catalog is used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eService Catalog product page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/resources/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-06-09T22:05:25Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/06/aws-service-catalog-now-available-jakarta-indonesia/","postDateTime":"2022-06-09T04:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog is now available in (Jakarta) Indonesia","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is now available to customers in the AWS Region in (Jakarta) Indonesia.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-05-aws-service-catalog-provisioning-constructs-aws-cloud-development-kit-aws-cdk-available","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/05/aws-service-catalog-provisioning-constructs-aws-cloud-development-kit-aws-cdk-available/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:51:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:20:09+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog Provisioning constructs for the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cdk/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK)\u003c/a\u003e are now available for builders to create application infrastructure in code that provisions cloud resources from their approved Service Catalog products. Service Catalog builders can now create their AWS CDK applications with approved constructs in familiar programming languages like Typescript and Python directly in their Integrated Development Environment. Using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/cdklabs/cdk-import\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ecdk-import\u003c/a\u003e, builders can access a library of Provisioning constructs in their local development environment for the AWS Service Catalog products they have access to provision which automatically include the governance that their administrators have configured. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFollowing inline guidance in their local development environment and automatically generated comments within their locally-installed constructs, builders can model complex application infrastructure that meets enterprise requirements with a few lines of code in a few minutes. When deploying CDK applications that contain one or more Provisioning constructs, AWS Service Catalog creates provisioned products reflective of those constructs and their configurations.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog Provisioning constructs are available through the cdk-import tool, which is available on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/cdklabs/cdk-import\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eGithub\u003c/a\u003e. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, see the following resources:\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/getstarted.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eGetting started with AWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cdk/latest/guide/getting_started.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eGetting started with the AWS CDK\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/cdklabs/cdk-import\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ecdk-import tool on GitHub\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003ca href\u003d\"https://constructs.dev/packages/@aws-cdk/aws-servicecatalog\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog Construct Library\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003ca href\u003d\"http://servicecatalog.workshop.aws/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog Workshop - Developers and Builders: Using Service Catalog with the AWS CDK\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-05-05T16:16:25Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/05/aws-service-catalog-provisioning-constructs-aws-cloud-development-kit-aws-cdk-available/","postDateTime":"2022-05-05T04:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Provisioning constructs for the AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) are now available","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog Provisioning constructs for the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/cdk.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK)\u003c/a\u003e are now available for builders to create application infrastructure in code that provisions cloud resources from their approved Service Catalog products. Service Catalog builders can now create their AWS CDK applications with approved constructs in familiar programming languages like Typescript and Python directly in their Integrated Development Environment. Using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/cdklabs/cdk-import\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ecdk-import\u003c/a\u003e, builders can access a library of Provisioning constructs in their local development environment for the AWS Service Catalog products they have access to provision which automatically include the governance that their administrators have configured. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-cloud-development-kit","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-cloud-development-kit","description":"general:products/aws-cloud-development-kit","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:55:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:55:46+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-04-aws-service-catalog-support-aws-cloud-development-kit-aws-cdk-available","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/04/aws-service-catalog-support-aws-cloud-development-kit-aws-cdk-available/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:34:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:32:46+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog constructs for the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cdk/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK)\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;are now available. Service Catalog administrators can now define their catalog in code within a CDK application that deploys through \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudformation/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS CloudFormation\u003c/a\u003e. They can also define a Service Catalog product entirely in code in CDK without having to upload and reference CloudFormation templates in Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) or AWS CodeCommit first.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog CDK constructs are available as a stable release in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://constructs.dev/packages/@aws-cdk/aws-servicecatalog\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog Construct Library\u003c/a\u003e and on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/aws/aws-cdk/tree/master/packages/%40aws-cdk/aws-servicecatalog\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eGitHub\u003c/a\u003e. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog CDK constructs enable Service Catalog administrators to use the AWS CDK to define, manage, maintain, and distribute their catalog in code. Service Catalog administrators can define infrastructure-as-code templates, organize their catalog with portfolios, add the right governance for their use, and distribute those portfolios to their teams.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, see the following resources:\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/getstarted.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eGetting started with AWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cdk/latest/guide/getting_started.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eGetting started with the AWS CDK\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003eAWS Service Catalog CDK Example Application: Catalog Builder – \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/aws-samples/aws-cdk-examples/tree/master/python/servicecatalog/portfolio-with-ec2-product\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ePython\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/aws-samples/aws-cdk-examples/tree/master/typescript/servicecatalog/portfolio-with-ec2-product\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eTypeScript\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://constructs.dev/packages/@aws-cdk/aws-servicecatalog\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog Construct Library\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"http://servicecatalog.workshop.aws/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog Workshop - Developers and Builders: Using Service\u0026nbsp;Catalog with the AWS CDK\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-04-28T21:20:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/04/aws-service-catalog-support-aws-cloud-development-kit-aws-cdk-available/","postDateTime":"2022-04-28T04:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog support for the AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) is now available","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog constructs for the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/cdk.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK)\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;are now available. Service Catalog administrators can now define their catalog in code within a CDK application that deploys through \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/cloudformation.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS CloudFormation\u003c/a\u003e. They can also define a Service Catalog product entirely in code in CDK without having to upload and reference CloudFormation templates in Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) or AWS CodeCommit first.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-cloud-development-kit","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-cloud-development-kit","description":"general:products/aws-cloud-development-kit","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:55:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:55:46+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-03-aws-service-catalog-new-console-feature","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/03/aws-service-catalog-new-console-feature/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:38:05+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:34:03+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Service Catalog is releasing a feature that helps to simplify builders’ access to the resources associated with their Provisioned Products. Previously, customers had to manually navigate through the AWS console to find a specific resource. With this feature, they can easily locate and access the resource of a provisioned product, right in the provisioned product detail page.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eIn the Provisioned Product detail console page, you will find a new tab called Resources that lists all your Provisioned Product’s underlying resources. If you want to work with a specific resource, just click on the resource link to access the resource’s dedicated console and perform subsequent actions on it. For example, you can navigate from one of your Provisioned Products in Service Catalog to one of its associated database instances with a single click.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis new feature is available via the Service Catalog console in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS commercial and GovCloud Regions\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, see Provisioned products in AWS Service Catalog.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-03-24T18:19:33Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/03/aws-service-catalog-new-console-feature/","postDateTime":"2022-03-24T05:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog announces a new console feature to directly access resources within a Provisioned Product","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Service Catalog is releasing a feature that helps to simplify builders’ access to the resources associated with their Provisioned Products. Previously, customers had to manually navigate through the AWS console to find a specific resource. With this feature, they can easily locate and access the resource of a provisioned product, right in the provisioned product detail page.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-03-service-catalog-now-supports-vpc-endpoint-policies","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/03/service-catalog-now-supports-vpc-endpoint-policies/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:34:38+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:08:38+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now supports Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) endpoint policies in all regions. Previously, Service Catalog supported integration with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/integrated-services-vpce-list.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e in all regions, where customers could use default policies that provided full access to Service Catalog.  With this newly supported feature, customers can create or modify their VPC endpoint(s), interface or gateway, and have the option of attaching a customer-managed policy that specifies access to Service Catalog. \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eService Catalog customers can leverage VPC endpoint policies as standalone AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) resource policies. If utilized, these policies do not override or replace an IAM user policy or Service Catalog-specific policies. This feature supports the ability for existing customers to continue using their default, full-access policies without having to make changes to their existing VPC configurations. \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eSupport for VPC endpoint policies is available in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eall regions where Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e is currently operating. To learn more, customers can reference documentation on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/servicecatalog.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eService Catalog endpoints and quotas\u003c/a\u003e as well as AWS documentation for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpc-endpoints-access.html#vpc-endpoint-policies\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003econtrolled access to services using VPC endpoints\u003c/a\u003e. For more information about Service Catalog, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eService Catalog product page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/resources/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-03-18T19:23:01Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/03/service-catalog-now-supports-vpc-endpoint-policies/","postDateTime":"2022-03-18T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Service Catalog now supports VPC Endpoint Policies","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now supports Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) endpoint policies in all regions. Previously, Service Catalog supported integration with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/integrated-services-vpce-list.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e in all regions, where customers could use default policies that provided full access to Service Catalog.  With this newly supported feature, customers can create or modify their VPC endpoint(s), interface or gateway, and have the option of attaching a customer-managed policy that specifies access to Service Catalog. \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-11-aws-service-management-connector-installation-easier-servicenow-guided-setup","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/aws-service-management-connector-installation-easier-servicenow-guided-setup/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:49:05+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:08:56+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can install the AWS Service Management Connector via a guided setup in ServiceNow. This guided setup simplifies the ServiceNow scoped app configurations tasks, minimizing the expertise needed to establish the connection between AWS and ServiceNow. ServiceNow administrators, or power users with permissions to the Connector scoped app, simply follow the guided steps and mark each task complete or skipped where applicable. The AWS Service Management Connector documentation also includes an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/baseline-permissions.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS CloudFormation baseline permissions\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;template that sets up the AWS environment. Thus, the ServiceNow Guide Setup and AWS baseline permissions give customers the ability to focus on developing guardrails and detective controls via integrated AWS services and validating that connection between AWS and ServiceNow.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis release also introduces a dual sync integration with AWS Support cases and ServiceNow incidents. ServiceNow change requests can also now be derived from AWS Systems Manager Change Manager templates, including executing curated automation playbooks upon approval. The connector provides existing integration features for AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config, AWS Systems Manager OpsCenter, AWS Systems Manager Automation and AWS Security Hub, which simplifies cloud provisioning, operations and resource management as well as enables you to view streamlined Service Management governance and oversight over AWS services.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow is available at no charge in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://store.servicenow.com/sn_appstore_store.do#!/store/application/f0b117a3db32320093a7d7a0cf961912/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eServiceNow Store\u003c/a\u003e. These new features are generally available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config, AWS Systems Manager and AWS Security Hub services are available. For more information, please visit the documentation on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/integrations-servicenow.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector\u003c/a\u003e. You can also learn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/config/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Config\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Systems Manager\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-support/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Support\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/security-hub/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Security Hub\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-11-18T18:52:13Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/11/aws-service-management-connector-installation-easier-servicenow-guided-setup/","postDateTime":"2021-11-18T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Management Connector makes installation easier through ServiceNow Guided Setup","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can install the AWS Service Management Connector via a guided setup in ServiceNow. This guided setup simplifies the ServiceNow scoped app configurations tasks, minimizing the expertise needed to establish the connection between AWS and ServiceNow. ServiceNow administrators, or power users with permissions to the Connector scoped app, simply follow the guided steps and mark each task complete or skipped where applicable. The AWS Service Management Connector documentation also includes an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/baseline-permissions.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS CloudFormation baseline permissions\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;template that sets up the AWS environment. Thus, the ServiceNow Guide Setup and AWS baseline permissions give customers the ability to focus on developing guardrails and detective controls via integrated AWS services and validating that connection between AWS and ServiceNow.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-09-aws-service-catalog-appregistry-aws-systems-manager","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/09/aws-service-catalog-appregistry-aws-systems-manager/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:30:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:28:31+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog AppRegistry and AWS Systems Manager Application Manager now provide an end-to-end AWS application management experience. With this release, customers can use AppRegistry to create applications within their infrastructure as code, CI/CD pipelines, and post-provisioning processes, and use Application Manager to view application operational data and perform operational actions.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eEnterprises are creating, migrating and managing thousands of applications on AWS that use hundreds of thousands of resources. Customers can now navigate directly from AppRegistry to Application Manager to view their AppRegistry application resources, monitor the application operational and compliance status, view operational items, and execute runbooks against application stacks or individual resources. AppRegistry creates a resource group for every application and CloudFormation stack associated to the application. The resource group is kept up-to-date with the application definition as resources are added and removed from the application. Application resource groups can be used with any \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ARG/latest/userguide/integrated-services-list.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS services that support resource groups\u003c/a\u003e, including Amazon CloudWatch Application Insights and Amazon CloudWatch automatic dashboards.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please refer to the documentation for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/appregistry.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog AppRegistry documentation\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/application-manager.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Systems Manager Application Manager.\u003c/a\u003e See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for Region availability.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-09-23T18:37:22Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/09/aws-service-catalog-appregistry-aws-systems-manager/","postDateTime":"2021-09-23T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Customers can now manage AWS Service Catalog AppRegistry applications in AWS Systems Manager","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog AppRegistry and AWS Systems Manager Application Manager now provide an end-to-end AWS application management experience. With this release, customers can use AppRegistry to create applications within their infrastructure as code, CI/CD pipelines, and post-provisioning processes, and use Application Manager to view application operational data and perform operational actions.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-09-aws-service-connector-servicenow-aws-catalog-appregistry","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/09/aws-service-connector-servicenow-aws-catalog-appregistry/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:35:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:21:25+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can view their registered applications on AWS Service Catalog AppRegistry in their ServiceNow CMDB leveraging the AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow. Organizations are creating, migrating, and managing applications on AWS that are associated with multiple AWS resources. Customers define applications within AppRegistry by providing a name, description, and associations to the AWS CloudFormation stacks and application metadata that constitute their application. With this integration, customers can view AWS applications in their ServiceNow system of record and operational tooling.  Customers can then relate ITSM process such as change requests, incidents/problem at the Application level in ServiceNow. This will allow for streamlined impact analysis and operational investigation of AWS applications.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis new version enables customers to configure, request and provision AWS Service Catalog products via ServiceNow order guides enabling customers to bundle multiple AWS services/stacks into a single service request. The connector also includes enhancements to AWS resource relationships from AWS Config into the ServiceNow CMDB.  The connector provides existing integration features for AWS Config, AWS Systems Manager OpsCenter, AWS Systems Manager Automation and AWS Security Hub, which simplifies cloud provisioning, operations and resource management for ServiceNow administrators.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow is available at no charge in the \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://store.servicenow.com/sn_appstore_store.do#!/store/application/f0b117a3db32320093a7d7a0cf961912/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eServiceNow Store\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e. These new features are generally available in all \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" style\u003d\"background-color: rgb(255,255,255);\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u0026nbsp;where AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config, AWS Systems Manager and AWS Security Hub services are available. For more information, please visit the documentation on the \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/integrations-servicenow.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" style\u003d\"background-color: rgb(255,255,255);\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e. You can also learn more about \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" style\u003d\"background-color: rgb(255,255,255);\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e, \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/config/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" style\u003d\"background-color: rgb(255,255,255);\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Config\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e, \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" style\u003d\"background-color: rgb(255,255,255);\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Systems Manager\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u0026nbsp;and \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/security-hub/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" style\u003d\"background-color: rgb(255,255,255);\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Security Hub\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-09-16T19:16:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/09/aws-service-connector-servicenow-aws-catalog-appregistry/","postDateTime":"2021-09-16T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":" AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow supports AWS Service Catalog AppRegistry","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can view their registered applications on AWS Service Catalog AppRegistry in their ServiceNow CMDB leveraging the AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow. Organizations are creating, migrating, and managing applications on AWS that are associated with multiple AWS resources. Customers define applications within AppRegistry by providing a name, description, and associations to the AWS CloudFormation stacks and application metadata that constitute their application. With this integration, customers can view AWS applications in their ServiceNow system of record and operational tooling.  Customers can then relate ITSM process such as change requests, incidents/problem at the Application level in ServiceNow. This will allow for streamlined impact analysis and operational investigation of AWS applications.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-systems-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-systems-manager","description":"general:products/aws-systems-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-09-aws-managed-services-ams-catalog-operational-on-demand","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/09/aws-managed-services-ams-catalog-operational-on-demand/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:30:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:10:30+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Managed Services (AMS) is excited to announce Operations on Demand, a flexible and scalable option to gain access to additional skilled AMS operations capacity, skills, and experience. Operations on Demand gives customers access to a full range of operational capabilities above and beyond the extensive scope provided by \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managedservices/latest/accelerate-guide/what-is-ams-op-plans.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAMS Operations Plans\u003c/a\u003e. Customers choose from a curated and continually expanding catalog of operational offerings which are delivered by a combination of automation and highly skilled AMS resources. The catalog includes a mix of short-term and ongoing operational use cases and can be used to supplement your existing operations or fill a knowledge or capacity gap. Examples of catalog offerings include assisting with the maintenance of Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS), operations of AWS Control Tower, management of SAP clusters, and performing in-place upgrades of instances running out-of-support operating systems. Customers pay for what they use in blocks of hours, and can unsubscribe from a catalog offering at any time. Please see our public documentation for a listing of current \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managedservices/latest/accelerate-guide/ood-catalog.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ecatalog offerings\u003c/a\u003e. The Operations on Demand feature is available for both the\u0026nbsp;AMS \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/managed-services/features/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAdvanced and Accelerate\u003c/a\u003e Operations Plans in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eregions\u003c/a\u003e where AMS is available.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managedservices/latest/accelerate-guide/ops-on-demand.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAMS documentation\u003c/a\u003e. Learn more about AMS \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/managed-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and download the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://pages.awscloud.com/forrester-tei-managed-service-2020.html?sc_icampaign\u003daware_forrester-total-economic-impact-study\u0026amp;sc_ichannel\u003dha\u0026amp;sc_icontent\u003dawssm-4873\u0026amp;sc_iplace\u003dbanner\u0026amp;trk\u003dha_awssm-4873\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eForrester Total Economic Impact™ study\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-09-08T18:49:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/09/aws-managed-services-ams-catalog-operational-on-demand/","postDateTime":"2021-09-08T16:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Managed Services (AMS) now offers a catalog of operational offerings with Operations on Demand","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Managed Services (AMS) is excited to announce Operations on Demand, a flexible and scalable option to gain access to additional skilled AMS operations capacity, skills, and experience. Operations on Demand gives customers access to a full range of operational capabilities above and beyond the extensive scope provided by \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managedservices/latest/accelerate-guide/what-is-ams-op-plans.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAMS Operations Plans\u003c/a\u003e. Customers choose from a curated and continually expanding catalog of operational offerings which are delivered by a combination of automation and highly skilled AMS resources. The catalog includes a mix of short-term and ongoing operational use cases and can be used to supplement your existing operations or fill a knowledge or capacity gap. Examples of catalog offerings include assisting with the maintenance of Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS), operations of AWS Control Tower, management of SAP clusters, and performing in-place upgrades of instances running out-of-support operating systems. Customers pay for what they use in blocks of hours, and can unsubscribe from a catalog offering at any time. Please see our public documentation for a listing of current \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/managedservices/latest/accelerate-guide/ood-catalog.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ecatalog offerings\u003c/a\u003e. The Operations on Demand feature is available for both the\u0026nbsp;AMS \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/managed-services/features.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAdvanced and Accelerate\u003c/a\u003e Operations Plans in all \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eregions\u003c/a\u003e where AMS is available.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-managed-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-managed-services","description":"general:products/aws-managed-services","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:45+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-07-aws-service-catalog-announces-improvements-getting-started-library","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/07/aws-service-catalog-announces-improvements-getting-started-library/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:42:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:20:01+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Service Catalog is releasing a new Getting Started Library (GSL) experience that simplifies discovering best practice templates and offers better guidance for Service Catalog Administrators when they use the library. The GSL contains more than 250 AWS best practice solutions for a wide variety of technical and business problems. The Library is regularly enriched with new solutions, with “New Relic AWS Control Tower Integration” or “Amazon EKS Architecture” as recent additions.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWhen Service Catalog Administrators navigate into the new GSL, they now have a direct access to search across all of the best practice templates from the GSL home page. They can search by keyword to find the template they need. For example, customers can search for “AI” and immediately access various templates such as “AI Powered Speech Analytics for Amazon Connect” or “AI-Powered Health Data Masking”. Once they find a relevant template for their use case, Service Catalog Administrators can now click on the “Add to portfolio” button and easily add the template to their catalog. A step-by-step explanation banner at the top of the page gives Service Catalog Administrators guidance on how to use the GSL to find a relevant template, organize their catalog with portfolios, add the right governance for their use, and distribute the templates with their teams. The new GSL allows customers to accelerate new workload creation efficiently and safely on AWS.\u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe new Getting Started Library is available via the Service Catalog console in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS commercial and GovCloud Regions\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/home?region\u003dus-east-1#getting-started-library\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGetting Started Library\u003c/a\u003e in AWS Service Catalog.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-07-28T17:44:26Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/07/aws-service-catalog-announces-improvements-getting-started-library/","postDateTime":"2021-07-28T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog announces improvements to the Getting Started Library","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Service Catalog is releasing a new Getting Started Library (GSL) experience that simplifies discovering best practice templates and offers better guidance for Service Catalog Administrators when they use the library. The GSL contains more than 250 AWS best practice solutions for a wide variety of technical and business problems. The Library is regularly enriched with new solutions, with “New Relic AWS Control Tower Integration” or “Amazon EKS Architecture” as recent additions.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-05-aws-security-hub-supports-bidirectional-integration-with-atlassian-jira-service-management","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/aws-security-hub-supports-bidirectional-integration-with-atlassian-jira-service-management/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:28:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:08:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/security-hub/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Security Hub\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now supports a bidirectional integration with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.atlassian.com/software/jira/service-management\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAtlassian Jira Service Management (JSM)\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp; You can now automatically create and update issues in Atlassian JSM from AWS Security Hub findings. Updates to those issues in Atlassian JSM will be synced with the findings in AWS Security Hub. This integration is available via the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/1221283/aws-service-management-connector-for-jsm?hosting\u003dserver\u0026amp;tab\u003doverview\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector for JSM\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;app. After downloading the app, you can decide if you want to send all findings, or only certain findings with specific severity levels to JSM. When you make an update to various fields in an issue, such as state or priority, those changes are automatically sent to AWS Security Hub so that AWS Security Hub always has the latest and correct information about that issue.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo see a demonstration of this integration, watch this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003duEKwu0M8S3M\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003evideo\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Service Management Connector for JSM is available at no charge in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/1221283/aws-service-management-connector-for-jsm?hosting\u003dserver\u0026amp;tab\u003doverview\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAtlassian Marketplace\u003c/a\u003e. This new feature is generally available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;where AWS Security Hub is available except in the AWS China (Beijing) Region operated by Sinnet and in the AWS China (Ningxia) Region operated by NWCD. For more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/integrations-jiraservicedesk.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e on the AWS Service Management Connector.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Service Management Connector for JSM also supports integrations with AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config, and AWS Systems Manager. You can also request and provision curated AWS products via AWS Service Catalog, view configuration item details on select resources within ServiceNow CMDB powered by AWS Config, and execute AWS Systems Manager automation documents via AWS Systems Manager Automation.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-regions.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAvailable globally\u003c/a\u003e, AWS Security Hub is designed to give you a comprehensive view of your security posture across your AWS accounts. With Security Hub, you now have a single place that aggregates, organizes, and prioritizes your security alerts, or findings, from multiple AWS services, such as Amazon GuardDuty, Amazon Inspector, Amazon Macie, AWS Firewall Manager, AWS System Manager Patch Manager, AWS IAM Access Analyzer, and from 55 AWS Partner solutions. You can also continuously monitor your environment using automated security checks based on standards, such as AWS Foundational Security Best Practices, the CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark, and the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard. You can also take action on these findings by investigating findings in Amazon Detective and by using Amazon CloudWatch Event rules to send the findings to ticketing, chat, Security Information and Event Management (SIEM), Security Orchestration Automation and Response (SOAR), incident management tools, and custom remediation playbooks.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eYou can enable your 30-day free trial of AWS Security Hub with a single-click in the AWS Management console. Please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Regional Services List\u003c/a\u003e for all the regions where AWS Security Hub is available. To learn more about AWS Security Hub capabilities, see the AWS Security Hub \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/what-is-securityhub.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e, and to start your 30-day free trial see the AWS Security Hub \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/security-hub/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003efree trial page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-06-04T19:24:46Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/aws-security-hub-supports-bidirectional-integration-with-atlassian-jira-service-management/","postDateTime":"2021-05-26T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Security Hub now supports bidirectional integration with Atlassian Jira Service Management","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/security-hub.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Security Hub\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now supports a bidirectional integration with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.atlassian.com/software/jira/service-management\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAtlassian Jira Service Management (JSM)\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp; You can now automatically create and update issues in Atlassian JSM from AWS Security Hub findings. Updates to those issues in Atlassian JSM will be synced with the findings in AWS Security Hub. This integration is available via the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/1221283/aws-service-management-connector-for-jsm?hosting\u003dserver\u0026amp;tab\u003doverview\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector for JSM\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;app. After downloading the app, you can decide if you want to send all findings, or only certain findings with specific severity levels to JSM. When you make an update to various fields in an issue, such as state or priority, those changes are automatically sent to AWS Security Hub so that AWS Security Hub always has the latest and correct information about that issue.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-security-hub","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-security-hub","description":"general:products/aws-security-hub","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:36+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-config","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-config","description":"general:products/aws-config","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#security-identity-and-compliance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"security-identity-and-compliance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/security-identity-and-compliance","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-systems-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-systems-manager","description":"general:products/aws-systems-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-04-aws-service-catalog-launches-a-console-experience-for-appregistry","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/04/aws-service-catalog-launches-a-console-experience-for-appregistry/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:39:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:28:28+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Service Catalog announces console support for AppRegistry applications. With this release, administrators can create and manage their application metadata in an easy-to-use console experience. AppRegistry is a feature of AWS Service Catalog, which is used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eEnterprises are creating, migrating and managing hundreds of applications on AWS that deploy thousands of resources. AWS Service Catalog AppRegistry provides a repository for organizing resource collections and managing application metadata on AWS. With this release, administrators can use the Service Catalog console to manage their applications, application metadata, and resource associations. Applications include the resource collections (CloudFormation Stacks) associated with the application, and attribute groups for describing applications on dimensions such as cost, compliance, security, and team ownership.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now use a combination of the AppRegistry console, CLI, API, and CloudFormation resources to manage their AppRegistry applications.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the Service Catalog product page and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/appregistry.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog AppRegistry documentation\u003c/a\u003e. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for region availability.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-04-23T15:29:48Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/04/aws-service-catalog-launches-a-console-experience-for-appregistry/","postDateTime":"2021-04-23T23:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog launches a console experience for AppRegistry","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Service Catalog announces console support for AppRegistry applications. With this release, administrators can create and manage their application metadata in an easy-to-use console experience. AppRegistry is a feature of AWS Service Catalog, which is used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-tools","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-tools","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-tools","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-04-aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-osaka","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/04/aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-osaka/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:40:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:07:03+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is now available to customers in the AWS Region in Osaka, Japan. AWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create, govern, and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eInstead of IT admins having to provision all of the cloud resources for their end users, AWS Service Catalog enables those users to manage and deploy IT services themselves. Enterprises can centrally curate and share commonly deployed IT services with teams to achieve consistent governance and meet compliance requirements. End users such as DevOps engineers and data scientists can quickly discover and self-service deploy the approved IT services that they need to use to perform their daily job functions. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith AWS Service Catalog you can control which IT services and versions are available, what is configured in each of the available services, and who gets permission access by individual, group, department or cost center. AWS Service Catalog is used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eService Catalog product page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/resources/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-04-22T20:55:52Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/04/aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-osaka/","postDateTime":"2021-04-22T17:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog is now available in Osaka","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is now available to customers in the AWS Region in Osaka, Japan. AWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create, govern, and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-12-aws-service-catalog-now-supports-tagoption-sharing","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/aws-service-catalog-now-supports-tagoption-sharing/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:07:02+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Service Catalog is releasing TagOption sharing, which enables administrators to distribute TagOptions when sharing portfolios to AWS accounts. TagOptions are key-value pairs used by administrators to define and enforce their tagging taxonomy. In their central account, administrators can define TagOptions and associate them to products and portfolios.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith TagOption sharing, administrators can now easily share TagOptions associated with portfolios and products with other accounts. When TagOptions are added or removed in the central account, that change is automatically reflected in recipient accounts. When an end user provisions a product that has TagOptions associated with it, they choose from a list of TagOption values that then become tags on the provisioned product. In recipients’ accounts administrators can associate additional local TagOptions to their imported portfolio to enforce tagging rules that are specific to that account.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eService Catalog TagOption Sharing is supported for both account-to-account sharing and Organizational sharing. It is available via the AWS API, CLI, and Service Catalog console in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS commercial and GovCloud Regions\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/catalogs_portfolios_sharing_how-to-share.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation on the Service Catalog Tag Option Sharing\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-12-28T21:56:54Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/aws-service-catalog-now-supports-tagoption-sharing/","postDateTime":"2020-12-24T14:45:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog now supports TagOption Sharing","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Service Catalog is releasing TagOption sharing, which enables administrators to distribute TagOptions when sharing portfolios to AWS accounts. TagOptions are key-value pairs used by administrators to define and enforce their tagging taxonomy. In their central account, administrators can define TagOptions and associate them to products and portfolios.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-12-provisioned-product-referencing-available-aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/provisioned-product-referencing-available-aws-service-catalog/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:08:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:15:28+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now supports referencing Service Catalog provisioned product outputs in new provisioned products or AWS CloudFormation stacks. Provisioned product outputs, such as a VPC identifier, can now be made available as inputs to dependent provisioned products and stacks. This saves time building applications that have dependencies on existing infrastructure, such as a VPC, S3 bucket, or RDS database.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith provisioned product referencing, you include a Service Catalog transform in your template. Each parameter your template references includes the name of the provisioned product and parameter. During provisioning, the Service Catalog transform retrieves the most recent output value from the referenced provisioned product. Multiple provisioned products and parameters can be referenced in your template.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSupport for Service Catalog provisioned product referencing is now available via the AWS API, CLI, and Service Catalog console in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS commercial Regions\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/transform-aws-servicecatalog.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation on Service Catalog provisioned product referencing\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-12-24T00:49:02Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/provisioned-product-referencing-available-aws-service-catalog/","postDateTime":"2020-12-23T12:54:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Provisioned product referencing is now available in AWS Service Catalog","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now supports referencing Service Catalog provisioned product outputs in new provisioned products or AWS CloudFormation stacks. Provisioned product outputs, such as a VPC identifier, can now be made available as inputs to dependent provisioned products and stacks. This saves time building applications that have dependencies on existing infrastructure, such as a VPC, S3 bucket, or RDS database.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-12-aws-security-hub-now-supports-bidirectional-integration-with-service-now-itsm","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/aws-security-hub-now-supports-bidirectional-integration-with-service-now-itsm/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:07:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:38:48+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/security-hub/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Security Hub\u003c/a\u003e now supports a bidirectional integration with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.servicenow.com/products/itsm.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eServiceNow ITSM\u003c/a\u003e, making it easier for Security Hub users to automatically create and update tickets in ServiceNow ITSM from Security Hub findings and ensure that updates to those tickets are synced with the findings. This integration is available via the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://store.servicenow.com/sn_appstore_store.do#!/store/application/f0b117a3db32320093a7d7a0cf961912/3.0.4?referer\u003d%2Fstore%2Fsearch%3Flistingtype%3Dallintegrations%25253Bancillary_app%25253Bcertified_apps%25253Bcontent%25253Bindustry_solution%25253Boem%26q%3Daws%2520service%2520catalog\u0026amp;sl\u003dsh\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow\u003c/a\u003e app. After downloading the app, you can decide if you want to send all or only certain findings with specific severity levels to ServiceNow and you can decide if you want to automatically create incident or problem tickets. Then, when you make an update to various fields in the ticket, such as state or priority, those changes are automatically sent to Security Hub, so that Security Hub always has the latest and correct information about that issue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can see a demonstration of this integration \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dOYTi0sjEggE\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow is available at no charge in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://store.servicenow.com/sn_appstore_store.do#!/store/application/f0b117a3db32320093a7d7a0cf961912/3.0.4?referer\u003d%2Fstore%2Fsearch%3Flistingtype%3Dallintegrations%25253Bancillary_app%25253Bcertified_apps%25253Bcontent%25253Bindustry_solution%25253Boem%26q%3Daws%2520service%2520catalog\u0026amp;sl\u003dsh\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eServiceNow Store\u003c/a\u003e. This new feature is generally available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Security Hub is available except in the AWS China (Beijing) Region operated by Sinnet and in the AWS China (Ningxia) Region operated by NWCD. For more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/integrations-servicenow.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e on the AWS Service Management Connector.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow also supports integrations with AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config, and AWS Systems Manager. You can also request and provision curated AWS products via AWS Service Catalog, view configuration item details on select resources within ServiceNow CMDB powered by AWS Config, and execute AWS Systems Manager automation documents via AWS Systems Manager Automation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-regions.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAvailable globally\u003c/a\u003e, AWS Security Hub is designed to give you a comprehensive view of your security posture across your AWS accounts. With Security Hub, you now have a single place that aggregates, organizes, and prioritizes your security alerts, or findings, from multiple AWS services, such as Amazon GuardDuty, Amazon Inspector, Amazon Macie, AWS Firewall Manager, AWS System Manager Patch Manager, AWS IAM Access Analyzer, and from 48 AWS Partner solutions. You can also continuously monitor your environment using automated security checks based on standards, such as AWS Foundational Security Best Practices, the CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark, and the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard. You can also take action on these findings by investigating findings in Amazon Detective and by using Amazon CloudWatch Event rules to send the findings to ticketing, chat, Security Information and Event Management (SIEM), Security Orchestration Automation and Response (SOAR), and incident management tools or to custom remediation playbooks.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can enable your 30-day free trial of AWS Security Hub with a single-click in the AWS Management console. Please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Regional Services List\u003c/a\u003e for all the regions where AWS Security Hub is available. To learn more about AWS Security Hub capabilities, see the AWS Security Hub \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/what-is-securityhub.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e, and to start your 30-day free trial see the AWS Security Hub \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/security-hub/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003efree trial page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003e\u003csup\u003eupdated on 1/3/22\u003c/sup\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-01-03T21:22:54Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/aws-security-hub-now-supports-bidirectional-integration-with-service-now-itsm/","postDateTime":"2020-12-11T16:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Security Hub now supports bidirectional integration with ServiceNow ITSM","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/security-hub.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Security Hub\u003c/a\u003e now supports a bidirectional integration with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.servicenow.com/products/itsm.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eServiceNow ITSM\u003c/a\u003e, making it easier for Security Hub users to automatically create and update tickets in ServiceNow ITSM from Security Hub findings and ensure that updates to those tickets are synced with the findings. This integration is available via the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://store.servicenow.com/sn_appstore_store.do#!/store/application/f0b117a3db32320093a7d7a0cf961912/3.0.4?referer\u003d%2Fstore%2Fsearch%3Flistingtype%3Dallintegrations%25253Bancillary_app%25253Bcertified_apps%25253Bcontent%25253Bindustry_solution%25253Boem%26q%3Daws%2520service%2520catalog\u0026amp;sl\u003dsh\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow\u003c/a\u003e app. After downloading the app, you can decide if you want to send all or only certain findings with specific severity levels to ServiceNow and you can decide if you want to automatically create incident or problem tickets. Then, when you make an update to various fields in the ticket, such as state or priority, those changes are automatically sent to Security Hub, so that Security Hub always has the latest and correct information about that issue.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-config","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-config","description":"general:products/aws-config","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-systems-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-systems-manager","description":"general:products/aws-systems-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-security-hub","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-security-hub","description":"general:products/aws-security-hub","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:36+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-12-simplify-provisioning-compute-resources-version3-5-aws-service-management-connector-servicenow","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/simplify-provisioning-compute-resources-version3-5-aws-service-management-connector-servicenow/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:09:21+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can view and select EC2 specific parameters (single and list) during provisioning from AWS accounts associated with the AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow, formerly known as the AWS Service Catalog Connector. Customers can also view consolidated cloud resources via AWS Config Aggregator within the ServiceNow CMDB, making it easier for ServiceNow administrators to see cloud resource transparency across AWS Accounts.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Connector enables end users to view EC2-specific parameters in ServiceNow during provisioning of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e﻿AWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e ﻿products, such as Availability Zones, Instance Id, KeyPair, Security Group, VPC, Subnet, Volume and Hosted Zone-Route53 - eliminating the need to hard code this information into CloudFormation templates.  ServiceNow administrators can also govern AWS resource tagging using tags from any ServiceNow table such as Cost Center, and Department during AWS Service Catalog product requests. Administrators can enforce their tagging taxonomy for downstream budget, cost allocation, and operational management of AWS resources.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/config/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e﻿AWS Config﻿\u003c/a\u003e features in the Connector for ServiceNow, admins and end-users can view aggregated cloud resource data across AWS account(s) and region(s) in the ServiceNow CMDB. For example, if you have a Config aggregator that aggregates Config data across accounts and regions into an account, you can synchronize this aggregated data from that account into your ServiceNow CMDB. ServiceNow administrators can also configure synchronization of select ServiceNow tables as custom resources within AWS Config to enable dual synchronization across both ServiceNow and AWS Config. This enables you to write Config rules against those custom resources and monitor compliance on a continuous basis. ServiceNow users can also view configuration items/relationships for cloud resources derived from AWS Config including OS level details (OS level details require AWS Systems Manager agents on resources).\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition to the new AWS Service Catalog and AWS Config features in this Connector release, ServiceNow users can also create and manage Security Findings as incidents or problems via \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/security-hub/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e﻿AWS Security Hub﻿\u003c/a\u003e and execute ﻿AWS Systems Manager﻿ automation documents via \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Systems Manager\u003c/a\u003e Automation directly within ServiceNow. This enables IT lifecycle management within ServiceNow using AWS native services.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow is available at no charge in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://store.servicenow.com/sn_appstore_store.do#!/store/application/f0b117a3db32320093a7d7a0cf961912/3.0.4?referer\u003d%2Fstore%2Fsearch%3Flistingtype%3Dallintegrations%25253Bancillary_app%25253Bcertified_apps%25253Bcontent%25253Bindustry_solution%25253Boem%26q%3Daws%2520service%2520catalog\u0026amp;sl\u003dsh\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e﻿ServiceNow Store﻿\u003c/a\u003e. This new feature is generally available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e﻿AWS Regions﻿\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config, AWS Systems Manager and AWS Security Hub services are available. To learn more, please visit the documentation on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/integrations-servicenow.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e﻿AWS Service Management Connector﻿\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-12-11T22:24:47Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/simplify-provisioning-compute-resources-version3-5-aws-service-management-connector-servicenow/","postDateTime":"2020-12-11T12:23:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Simplify EC2 provisioning and viewing cloud resources in the ServiceNow CMDB with AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can view and select EC2 specific parameters (single and list) during provisioning from AWS accounts associated with the AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow, formerly known as the AWS Service Catalog Connector. Customers can also view consolidated cloud resources via AWS Config Aggregator within the ServiceNow CMDB, making it easier for ServiceNow administrators to see cloud resource transparency across AWS Accounts.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-systems-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-systems-manager","description":"general:products/aws-systems-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-security-hub","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-security-hub","description":"general:products/aws-security-hub","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:36+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-config","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-config","description":"general:products/aws-config","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-12-customers-use-aws-service-catalog-appregistry-define-describe-aws-applications","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/customers-use-aws-service-catalog-appregistry-define-describe-aws-applications/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:16:54+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog AppRegistry provides a place to collect your AWS CloudFormation stacks and associate your customer-defined attribute groups (metadata) that describe your AWS applications. Customers can automate updates of stack and metadata changes by calling AppRegistry from within their CI/CD processes. IT and business stakeholders have up-to-date information on their applications, such as organizational ownership, data sensitivity, and cost center.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBuilders define their applications within AppRegistry by providing a  name, description, and associations to attribute groups and  CloudFormation stacks that are part of their application. The associated attribute groups, which are customer-defined JSON files, represent the metadata that your enterprise teams, including application teams, finance, security, and central IT teams, create and manage for the application. Attribute groups can also be defined by software partners, enabling centralization of application metadata across teams and software tooling. Resources (CloudFormation stacks) can also be associated to the application, including across environments like development, test, and production, and stacks used to manage the application like pipelines. This provides a central location for collecting all stacks and metadata for an application. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAppRegistry is available via the AWS API and CLI in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS commercial Regions\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/dg/API_Operations_AWS_Service_Catalog_App_Registry.html\"\u003edocumentation on the Service Catalog AppRegistry API\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-12-03T17:55:32Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/12/customers-use-aws-service-catalog-appregistry-define-describe-aws-applications/","postDateTime":"2020-12-03T15:29:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Customers can now use AWS Service Catalog AppRegistry to define and describe their AWS applications","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog AppRegistry provides a place to collect your AWS CloudFormation stacks and associate your customer-defined attribute groups (metadata) that describe your AWS applications. Customers can automate updates of stack and metadata changes by calling AppRegistry from within their CI/CD processes. IT and business stakeholders have up-to-date information on their applications, such as organizational ownership, data sensitivity, and cost center.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#reinvent-2020-partner","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"reinvent-2020-partner","description":"marketing:marchitecture/reinvent-2020-partner","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:58:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:58:28+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-11-aws-customer-can-now-use-aws-service-catalog-stack-import-to-add-governance","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/aws-customer-can-now-use-aws-service-catalog-stack-import-to-add-governance/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:08:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:37:10+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog administrators can now add Service Catalog governance to their existing AWS CloudFormation stacks. Once imported into Service Catalog, administrators can manage stack updates, govern parameters, and enforce tagging. With this new feature, long-running stacks can be governed while leaving the underlying resources untouched. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith stack import, administrators create Service Catalog products with templates from CloudFormation that match their running stacks. Administrators establish governance by associating constraints and tag options to the products used for import. End users import a CloudFormation stack, creating a Service Catalog provisioned product. When the import is complete, end-users can update, terminate, and perform operational actions on their imported provisioned products. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eService Catalog Stack Import is available via the AWS API, CLI, and Service Catalog console in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS commercial and GovCloud Regions\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, read the documentation on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/dg/API_ImportAsProvisionedProduct.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eService Catalog stack import API\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-11-18T16:27:18Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/aws-customer-can-now-use-aws-service-catalog-stack-import-to-add-governance/","postDateTime":"2020-11-17T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Customers can now use AWS Service Catalog stack import to add governance to their existing AWS CloudFormation stacks","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog administrators can now add Service Catalog governance to their existing AWS CloudFormation stacks. Once imported into Service Catalog, administrators can manage stack updates, govern parameters, and enforce tagging. With this new feature, long-running stacks can be governed while leaving the underlying resources untouched. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-11-aws-service-catalog-supports-stackset-instance-operations","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/aws-service-catalog-supports-stackset-instance-operations/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:06:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:08:16+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now supports Stack Set instance operations. With this new feature, end-users can control the individual instances for their StackSets, within the constraints specified by their AWS Service Catalog administrator.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEnd-users can easily specify the accounts and regions for provisioning and termination of individual instances in their StackSet. They can add or remove the regions and accounts where their instances are running, which will then provision or terminate instance(s) in the specified accounts and/or regions. Updates to a StackSet will still apply to all instances, regardless of region or account. The administrator still controls the available accounts and regions via a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/constraints-stackset.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eStackSet constraint.\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSupport for Stack Set instance operations in Service Catalog is now available via the AWS API, CLI, and Service Catalog console in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS commercial and GovCloud Regions\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/userguide/enduser-stack-constraint.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ethe documentation on Service Catalog StackSet instance operations\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-11-04T23:12:05Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/aws-service-catalog-supports-stackset-instance-operations/","postDateTime":"2020-11-04T13:21:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog now supports StackSet instance operations ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now supports Stack Set instance operations. With this new feature, end-users can control the individual instances for their StackSets, within the constraints specified by their AWS Service Catalog administrator.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-10-aws-service-catalog-now-provides-one-page-provisioning-with-a-new-console-experience","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/aws-service-catalog-now-provides-one-page-provisioning-with-a-new-console-experience/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:12:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:13:44+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now provides simplified provisioning of cloud resources with a one-page launch process and a new console experience. With this new feature, end-users can more easily and quickly provision products with fewer errors. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe new console provides end-users with a single page of information they need to provision products provided by their cloud administrators. With the one-page launch process, required parameters are more evident. Users may still explore and modify optional configurations. The console also provides a new, consistent AWS Service Catalog experience for both administrators and end-users.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe new console is available in all AWS Service Catalog \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eregions\u003c/a\u003e. You can learn more about AWS Service Catalog \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-10-29T21:02:30Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/aws-service-catalog-now-provides-one-page-provisioning-with-a-new-console-experience/","postDateTime":"2020-10-29T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog now provides One-Page Provisioning with a new console experience","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now provides simplified provisioning of cloud resources with a one-page launch process and a new console experience. With this new feature, end-users can more easily and quickly provision products with fewer errors. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-10-simplify-provisioning-of-compute-resources-with-version-1-7-of-the-aws-service-management-connector-for-jira-service-desk","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/simplify-provisioning-of-compute-resources-with-version-1-7-of-the-aws-service-management-connector-for-jira-service-desk/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:11:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:28:12+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, Jira Service Desk users can view EC2 specific parameters from AWS accounts associated with version 1.7 of the AWS Service Management Connector for Jira Service Desk, simplifying the provisioning of compute resources. End users can now view parameters such as  Availability Zones, Instance IDs, Key Pairs, and Security Groups directly in Jira Service Desk during provisioning, eliminating the need to find this information in other consoles or have them coded directly into CloudFormation templates.  \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJira Service Desk administrators can also configure the AWS request type form components available for end users to view as well as assign the admin user used by Jira’s workflow engine.  This simplifies the user experience by displaying the right information to users provisioning of cloud resources.  The AWS Service Management Connector for JSD also integrates AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config, and AWS Systems Manager to provide governance and lifecycle management of AWS products. Administrators can view configuration item details on provisioned products via AWS Config, create and manage operational items via AWS Systems Manager OpsCenter, and execute AWS Systems Manager automation documents within Jira Service Desk.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Service Management Connector for Jira Service Desk is available at no charge in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://marketplace.atlassian.com/1221283\"\u003eAtlassian Marketplace\u003c/a\u003e. This new feature is generally available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config, and AWS Systems Manager services are available. For more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/integrations-jiraservicedesk.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. You can also learn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/config/\"\u003eAWS Config\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/\"\u003eAWS Systems Manager\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-10-29T19:51:50Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/simplify-provisioning-of-compute-resources-with-version-1-7-of-the-aws-service-management-connector-for-jira-service-desk/","postDateTime":"2020-10-29T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Simplify provisioning of compute resources with version 1.7 of the AWS Service Management Connector for Jira Service Desk ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, Jira Service Desk users can view EC2 specific parameters from AWS accounts associated with version 1.7 of the AWS Service Management Connector for Jira Service Desk, simplifying the provisioning of compute resources. End users can now view parameters such as  Availability Zones, Instance IDs, Key Pairs, and Security Groups directly in Jira Service Desk during provisioning, eliminating the need to find this information in other consoles or have them coded directly into CloudFormation templates.  \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-systems-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-systems-manager","description":"general:products/aws-systems-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-config","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-config","description":"general:products/aws-config","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-09-service-catalog-simplifies-product-discovery-provisioning-and-search","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/service-catalog-simplifies-product-discovery-provisioning-and-search/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:55:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:19:20+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now supports the use of administrator-provided names for product discovery, provisioning, and searches on running products. With this new feature, administrators can define their taxonomy for product naming and versioning, and this taxonomy is accessible to builders and administrators for use within their code and scripts. Referencing by name helps builders innovate faster, and provides a consistent product discovery and provisioning experience across accounts and regions. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog is used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Service Catalog API Describe Product, Describe Provisioning Parameters, Provision Product, Update Provision Product, and Search Provisioned Products now support the use of administrator-defined product and version names. Product provisioning is further simplified by supporting the inclusion of the portfolio name, which is also administrator-defined, and establishes the governance enforced at provisioning. Customers can access these features via API, CLI, and CloudFormation resources. Administrators and builders can search for running products within their account and region based on administrator-provided product and version names, making it possible to find running products that share a similar name space or version number. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe simplified Service Catalog API and CloudFormation resource is now available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS commercial and GovCloud Regions\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/dg/service-catalog-api-overview.html\"\u003ethe Service Catalog Developer Guide – API Overview\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-09-09T21:13:24Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/service-catalog-simplifies-product-discovery-provisioning-and-search/","postDateTime":"2020-09-09T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Service Catalog simplifies product discovery, provisioning, and search","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now supports the use of administrator-provided names for product discovery, provisioning, and searches on running products. With this new feature, administrators can define their taxonomy for product naming and versioning, and this taxonomy is accessible to builders and administrators for use within their code and scripts. Referencing by name helps builders innovate faster, and provides a consistent product discovery and provisioning experience across accounts and regions. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-07-aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-africa-cape-town-and-europe-milan","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-africa-cape-town-and-europe-milan/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:00:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:17:54+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is now available in two new AWS Regions. With this release, AWS Service Catalog is now available in 21 regions including US East (N. Virginia, Ohio), US West (N. California, Oregon), Canada (Central), South America (São Paulo), Europe (Ireland, Frankfurt, London, Paris, Stockholm and Milan), South America (Sao Paulo), Middle East (Bahrain) and Asia Pacific (Mumbai, Seoul, Singapore, Sydney, Hong Kong, and Tokyo) and Africa (Cape Town). AWS Service Catalog is also available in GovCloud (US-West) and GovCloud (US-East) Regions, AWS Regions designed to host sensitive data and regulated workloads in the cloud for customers who have U.S. federal, state, and local government compliance requirements.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog enables organizations on AWS to create, govern, and manage a catalog of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog allows you to centrally manage commonly deployed IT services, and helps you to achieve consistent governance and meet your compliance requirements, while enabling users to quickly deploy only the approved IT services that they need.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-07-15T17:13:35Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-africa-cape-town-and-europe-milan/","postDateTime":"2020-07-15T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog is now available in Africa (Cape Town) and Europe (Milan)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is now available in two new AWS Regions. With this release, AWS Service Catalog is now available in 21 regions including US East (N. Virginia, Ohio), US West (N. California, Oregon), Canada (Central), South America (São Paulo), Europe (Ireland, Frankfurt, London, Paris, Stockholm and Milan), South America (Sao Paulo), Middle East (Bahrain) and Asia Pacific (Mumbai, Seoul, Singapore, Sydney, Hong Kong, and Tokyo) and Africa (Cape Town). AWS Service Catalog is also available in GovCloud (US-West) and GovCloud (US-East) Regions, AWS Regions designed to host sensitive data and regulated workloads in the cloud for customers who have U.S. federal, state, and local government compliance requirements.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#internet-of-things","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"internet-of-things","description":"marketing:marchitecture/internet-of-things","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-07-provisioned-product-outputs-now-available-aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/provisioned-product-outputs-now-available-aws-service-catalog/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:09:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:16:05+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now supports obtaining outputs from a Service Catalog provisioned product in an AWS CloudFormation template. Product outputs provide the interface from one product to another. With this new feature, administrators and developers can easily refer to those outputs in order to combine the products needed for their applications, which saves time building applications that use more than one product, such as a three-tier web application.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith provisioned product outputs, administrators and developers can now combine products that depend on each other in a CloudFormation template. Outputs from each provisioned product are available as inputs into other products and AWS resources in the template.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSupport for provisioned product outputs in Service Catalog is now available via the AWS API, CLI, and Service Catalog console in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS commercial and GovCloud Regions\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-resource-servicecatalog-cloudformationprovisionedproduct.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ethe documentation on Service Catalog provisioned product outputs\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-07-10T17:17:32Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/provisioned-product-outputs-now-available-aws-service-catalog/","postDateTime":"2020-07-10T12:58:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Provisioned product outputs are now available in AWS Service Catalog","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now supports obtaining outputs from a Service Catalog provisioned product in an AWS CloudFormation template. Product outputs provide the interface from one product to another. With this new feature, administrators and developers can easily refer to those outputs in order to combine the products needed for their applications, which saves time building applications that use more than one product, such as a three-tier web application.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-06-aws-service-catalog-now-supports-sharing-portfolios-across-an-organization-from-a-delegated-member-account","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/06/aws-service-catalog-now-supports-sharing-portfolios-across-an-organization-from-a-delegated-member-account/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:05+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:07:57+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Service Catalog is releasing delegated administrator portfolio sharing, which enables administrators to more easily distribute and manage AWS services across multiple AWS accounts. Service Catalog administrators can now share services from multiple member accounts within their AWS Organization. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this new feature, administrators can designate specific member accounts to share Service Catalog portfolios with their organization. Each of these accounts becomes a hub in the Service Catalog hub-and-spoke sharing model. Hub account administrators can share portfolios to any organizational unit or member account. Spoke account administrators then provide end-users with access to imported portfolios. This provides Service Catalog administrators with the flexibility to create and manage multiple hub accounts for sharing AWS services within their organization. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eService Catalog delegated administrator portfolio sharing is available via the AWS API, CLI, and Service Catalog console in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS commercial and GovCloud Regions\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/catalogs_portfolios_sharing.html\"\u003edocumentation on Service Catalog portfolio sharing\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-06-12T18:59:33Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/06/aws-service-catalog-now-supports-sharing-portfolios-across-an-organization-from-a-delegated-member-account/","postDateTime":"2020-06-12T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog now supports sharing portfolios across an organization from a delegated member account","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Service Catalog is releasing delegated administrator portfolio sharing, which enables administrators to more easily distribute and manage AWS services across multiple AWS accounts. Service Catalog administrators can now share services from multiple member accounts within their AWS Organization. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-organizations","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-organizations","description":"general:products/aws-organizations","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-06-simplify-cloud-resource-management-with-aws-service-management-connector-for-servicenow","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/06/simplify-cloud-resource-management-with-aws-service-management-connector-for-servicenow/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:28:22+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, we’re excited to announce the AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow, formerly known as the AWS Service Catalog Connector. The AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow enables integration features for AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config, and AWS Systems Manager within ServiceNow. This simplifies cloud provisioning and resource management for ServiceNow administrators, and also makes it easier for ServiceNow users to request AWS products, which can be any IT service that administrators want to make available for deployment on AWS.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this integration, ServiceNow administrators can provide pre-approved and compliant, AWS resources to end-users using AWS Service Catalog, execute automation playbooks using AWS Systems Manager, and track resources in the ServiceNow CMDB using AWS Config within ServiceNow. This simplifies AWS product request actions for ServiceNow users and provides governance and oversight over AWS products via ServiceNow. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow is available at no charge in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://store.servicenow.com/sn_appstore_store.do#!/store/application/f0b117a3db32320093a7d7a0cf961912/3.0.4?referer\u003d%2Fstore%2Fsearch%3Flistingtype%3Dallintegrations%25253Bancillary_app%25253Bcertified_apps%25253Bcontent%25253Bindustry_solution%25253Boem%26q%3Daws%2520service%2520catalog\u0026amp;sl\u003dsh\"\u003eServiceNow Store\u003c/a\u003e. This new feature is generally available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config, and AWS Systems Manager services are available. For more information, please visit the documentation on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/integrations-servicenow.html\"\u003eAWS Service Management Connector\u003c/a\u003e. You can also learn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/config/\"\u003eAWS Config\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/\"\u003eAWS Systems Manager\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-06-16T20:45:26Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/06/simplify-cloud-resource-management-with-aws-service-management-connector-for-servicenow/","postDateTime":"2020-06-12T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Simplify cloud resource management with AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, we’re excited to announce the AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow, formerly known as the AWS Service Catalog Connector. The AWS Service Management Connector for ServiceNow enables integration features for AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config, and AWS Systems Manager within ServiceNow. This simplifies cloud provisioning and resource management for ServiceNow administrators, and also makes it easier for ServiceNow users to request AWS products, which can be any IT service that administrators want to make available for deployment on AWS.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-config","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-config","description":"general:products/aws-config","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-systems-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-systems-manager","description":"general:products/aws-systems-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#applications","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"applications","description":"marketing:marchitecture/applications","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-05-parameter-support-now-available-with-service-actions-aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/parameter-support-now-available-with-service-actions-aws-service-catalog/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:01:32+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:03:33+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog administrators can now create service actions that use AWS Systems Manager Automation documents with more than one parameter. With this new feature, Service Catalog end users can now execute more complex operational tasks, such as creating a backup or filing a ticket based on content they provided. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith service actions, administrators can enable end users to securely perform operational tasks on their own, troubleshoot issues, run approved commands, or request permissions in Service Catalog. With parameter support, administrators can now enable end-users to securely perform a wider range of operational tasks. Administrators define parameters to be collected and used in their Systems Manager Automation document. Administrators then associate the service action to one or more products, so that when an end user provisions the product, the service action is available. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eParameter support for Service Catalog service actions is available via the AWS API, CLI, and Service Catalog console in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS commercial and GovCloud Regions\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/using-service-actions.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e on Service Catalog service actions.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-05-08T17:51:22Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/parameter-support-now-available-with-service-actions-aws-service-catalog/","postDateTime":"2020-05-08T10:28:12Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Parameter support is now available with service actions in AWS Service Catalog","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog administrators can now create service actions that use AWS Systems Manager Automation documents with more than one parameter. With this new feature, Service Catalog end users can now execute more complex operational tasks, such as creating a backup or filing a ticket based on content they provided. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-04-aws-service-catalog-adds-three-new-getting-started-portfolios","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/aws-service-catalog-adds-three-new-getting-started-portfolios/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:32+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:24:28+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e has added three new portfolios to the Getting Started Library that enable customers to build faster on AWS. These new portfolios include AWS Quick Starts, AWS Solutions, and AWS Config Conformance Packs, with a total of 30 new well-architected implementations and blueprints for solving common enterprise cloud needs. Service Catalog Administrators can share these implementations and blueprints with their teams, providing developer self-service while staying compliant with organizational best practices and policies. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Quick Starts portfolio helps you accelerate the implementation of your AWS Marketplace solutions. It includes 15 Quick Start templates for AWS Marketplace products such as Aviatrix, BIG-IP, Chef, Fortinet, Splunk, TIBCO, Trend Micro, and more. The AWS Solutions portfolio includes 11 implementations that enable admins to quickly establish a secure set of capabilities in multiple domain areas, including centralized logging, limit monitoring, web application firewall security automation, distributed load testing, server fleet management, and serverless image handling. The AWS Config Conformance Packs portfolio helps customers implement automated AWS resource conformance for Amazon DynamoDB, AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM), and PCI DSS. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt\u0027s easy to get started. You can find the new portfolios in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://us-east-1.console.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/home?isSceuc\u003dfalse\u0026amp;region\u003dus-east-1#portfolios?activeTab\u003dgslAdminPortfolios\"\u003eGetting Started Library\u003c/a\u003e in the AWS Service Catalog console. The new portfolios are available in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e in which Service Catalog is available. Using blueprints may require subscriptions to third-party software products through AWS Marketplace, and you will be charged for AWS resources used. To learn more, visit the AWS Service Catalog Getting Started Library \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/getting-started-library.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-04-28T22:59:59Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/aws-service-catalog-adds-three-new-getting-started-portfolios/","postDateTime":"2020-04-28T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog adds three new Getting Started portfolios","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/servicecatalog.html\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e has added three new portfolios to the Getting Started Library that enable customers to build faster on AWS. These new portfolios include AWS Quick Starts, AWS Solutions, and AWS Config Conformance Packs, with a total of 30 new well-architected implementations and blueprints for solving common enterprise cloud needs. Service Catalog Administrators can share these implementations and blueprints with their teams, providing developer self-service while staying compliant with organizational best practices and policies. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-04-local-launch-contraints-now-generally-available-in-aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/local-launch-contraints-now-generally-available-in-aws-service-catalog/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:05:28+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now supports local launch constraints. With this new feature, administrators can share products from one AWS account to other AWS accounts, and have those products launch locally in each account. In Service Catalog, this is referred to as a hub-and-spoke model of sharing approved IT services. This makes it easier for administrators to distribute and manage these services across multiple accounts, providing self-service access while staying compliant with organizational best practices and policies.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Service Catalog local launch constraints, administrators perform all governance setup in the hub account. They create a hub account local launch constraint, associate it to the portfolio that contains the products they want to distribute, and then share that portfolio to target spoke accounts. When end users provision products from the imported portfolio, they are provisioned in their spoke account. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eService Catalog local launch constraints are available via the AWS API, CLI, console, and AWS CloudFormation resources in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS commercial and GovCloud Regions\u003c/a\u003e. There is no additional charge for using Service Catalog local launch constraints. Learn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/catalogs_portfolios_sharing.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eService Catalog portfolio sharing\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-04-08T22:16:51Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/local-launch-contraints-now-generally-available-in-aws-service-catalog/","postDateTime":"2020-04-08T12:14:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Local launch constraints are now generally available in AWS Service Catalog","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now supports local launch constraints. With this new feature, administrators can share products from one AWS account to other AWS accounts, and have those products launch locally in each account. In Service Catalog, this is referred to as a hub-and-spoke model of sharing approved IT services. This makes it easier for administrators to distribute and manage these services across multiple accounts, providing self-service access while staying compliant with organizational best practices and policies.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-03-simplify-cloud-resource-management-with-aws-service-management-connector-for-jira-service-desk","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/03/simplify-cloud-resource-management-with-aws-service-management-connector-for-jira-service-desk/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:00:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:00:20+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, we announce the AWS Service Management Connector for Jira Service Desk, formerly known as the AWS Service Catalog Connector. The AWS Service Management Connector for Jira Service Desk enables AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config, and AWS Systems Manager integration features on Jira projects. This capability simplifies cloud provisioning and resource management for Jira Service Desk administrators, and makes it easier for Jira Service Desk users to request AWS products, which can be any IT service that administrators want to make available for deployment on AWS and third-party resources.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJira Service Desk administrators can configure the connector to work with existing or new AWS accounts and roles. Users and admins can also view configuration item details from AWS Config on provisioned products and execute AWS Systems Manager automation documents within Jira Service Desk. This streamlines AWS provisioning, resource transparency and automation in familiar tools for end users such as the Jira Service Desk software.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, Jira Service Desk administrators can open their Jira instance, select Add-ons, then find and install the AWS Service Management Connector for Jira Service Desk. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Service Management Connector for Jira Service Desk is available at no charge in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://marketplace.atlassian.com/1221283\"\u003eAtlassian Marketplace\u003c/a\u003e. The connector is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where Service Catalog, Config, and Systems Manager are available. For more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/integrations-jiraservicedesk.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-04-01T17:47:18Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/03/simplify-cloud-resource-management-with-aws-service-management-connector-for-jira-service-desk/","postDateTime":"2020-03-31T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Simplify cloud resource management with AWS Service Management Connector for Jira Service Desk","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, we announce the AWS Service Management Connector for Jira Service Desk, formerly known as the AWS Service Catalog Connector. The AWS Service Management Connector for Jira Service Desk enables AWS Service Catalog, AWS Config, and AWS Systems Manager integration features on Jira projects. This capability simplifies cloud provisioning and resource management for Jira Service Desk administrators, and makes it easier for Jira Service Desk users to request AWS products, which can be any IT service that administrators want to make available for deployment on AWS and third-party resources.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-administration","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-administration","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-administration","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:00:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:00:46+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-config","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-config","description":"general:products/aws-config","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-management-console","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-management-console","description":"general:products/aws-management-console","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-tools","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-tools","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-tools","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-03-aws-service-catalog-quotas-can-now-be-managed-through-aws-service-quotas","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/03/aws-service-catalog-quotas-can-now-be-managed-through-aws-service-quotas/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:02:41+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog administrators can now view and manage their Service Catalog service quotas through AWS Service Quotas. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eService Quotas helps you to view and manage service quota information centrally for your AWS services. Now, you can use the Service Quotas console, AWS Command Line Interface, and AWS SDK to view service quota information for AWS Service Catalog, such as the number of products per portfolio and the number of product versions per product.  There is no additional cost to view AWS Service Catalog quota information in Service Quotas. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog is used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is available in all commercial and GovCloud regions. AWS Service Quotas is available in US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (N. California), US West (Oregon), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Asia Pacific (Osaka), Canada (Central), EU (Frankfurt), EU (Ireland), EU (London), EU (Paris) and South America (São Paulo). \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLearn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/limits.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicequotas/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Quotas\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-03-26T16:59:21Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/03/aws-service-catalog-quotas-can-now-be-managed-through-aws-service-quotas/","postDateTime":"2020-03-26T12:47:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog quotas can now be managed through AWS Service Quotas","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog administrators can now view and manage their Service Catalog service quotas through AWS Service Quotas. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-03-aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-east-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/03/aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-east-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:00:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:00:01+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e in the AWS GovCloud (US-East) Region, an AWS Region designed to host sensitive data and regulated workloads in the cloud for customers who have U.S. federal, state, and local government compliance requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog allows you to centrally manage commonly deployed IT services, and helps you achieve consistent governance and meet your compliance requirements, while enabling users to quickly deploy only the approved IT services they need.\u003cbr\u003e\nLearn more about the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US)\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-03-26T18:36:48Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/03/aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-east-region/","postDateTime":"2020-03-26T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog is now available in the AWS GovCloud (US-East) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/servicecatalog.html\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e in the AWS GovCloud (US-East) Region, an AWS Region designed to host sensitive data and regulated workloads in the cloud for customers who have U.S. federal, state, and local government compliance requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-02-aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-hong-kong-and-bahrain","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/02/aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-hong-kong-and-bahrain/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:01:32+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:07:26+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is new available to customers in the AWS Bahrain and Hong Kong regions. AWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. Enterprises can centrally curate and share IT services with teams to achieve consistent governance and meet compliance requirements. Users can self-service discover and deploy only the approved IT services they need.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eService Catalog product page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/resources/\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-02-26T19:39:46Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/02/aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-hong-kong-and-bahrain/","postDateTime":"2020-02-26T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog is now available in Hong Kong and Bahrain","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is new available to customers in the AWS Bahrain and Hong Kong regions. AWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. Enterprises can centrally curate and share IT services with teams to achieve consistent governance and meet compliance requirements. Users can self-service discover and deploy only the approved IT services they need.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#internet-of-things","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"internet-of-things","description":"marketing:marchitecture/internet-of-things","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-12-aws-service-catalog-supports-deprecation-product-versions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/aws-service-catalog-supports-deprecation-product-versions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:07:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:31:10+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Service Catalog announces support for the deprecation of product versions. With the release of product version guidance, administrators can prevent new launches of a product version while allowing their use and updates in existing stacks.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing Service Catalog version guidance, you can set a product version as deprecated using the API, CLI, or console. Once a version is deprecated, only users with running stacks of that version are able to use it. The version is not available for users provisioning new stacks. If you wish to prevent all use of a product version, including updates, they you can make the version inactive. This feature is available in all commercial and GovCloud regions where AWS Service Catalog is available. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog is used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS.  \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLearn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/dg/API_ProvisioningArtifactDetail.html\"\u003eproduct version guidance\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-12-18T17:22:45Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/aws-service-catalog-supports-deprecation-product-versions/","postDateTime":"2019-12-18T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog supports deprecation of product versions ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Service Catalog announces support for the deprecation of product versions. With the release of product version guidance, administrators can prevent new launches of a product version while allowing their use and updates in existing stacks.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-11-aws-service-catalog-adds-high-reliability-architectures-getting-started-library","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/aws-service-catalog-adds-high-reliability-architectures-getting-started-library/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:19:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:52:44+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  Today, AWS announces a High Reliability Architectures portfolio available in AWS Service Catalog. This new portfolio contains 7 blueprints for building high reliability applications on AWS. The Getting Started Library in AWS Service Catalog provides well-architected blueprints for using AWS services.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe example blueprints include layers for identity, object store, data,  presentation, and application. In addition there is an infrastructure  pipeline for staging pre-production and production deployments, and an  application architecture example that ties the layers together in a  sample high reliability application. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eService Catalog\u003c/a\u003e is used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and distribute approved applications on AWS. The new High Reliability Architectures are available in all AWS Service Catalog commercial and GovCloud regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLearn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-11-25T20:25:22Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/aws-service-catalog-adds-high-reliability-architectures-getting-started-library/","postDateTime":"2019-11-25T09:47:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog adds High Reliability Architectures to the Getting Started Library","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  Today, AWS announces a High Reliability Architectures portfolio available in AWS Service Catalog. This new portfolio contains 7 blueprints for building high reliability applications on AWS. The Getting Started Library in AWS Service Catalog provides well-architected blueprints for using AWS services.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#security-identity-and-compliance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"security-identity-and-compliance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/security-identity-and-compliance","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-11-simplify-cloud-provisioning-with-aws-service-catalog-connector-for-jira-service-desk","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/simplify-cloud-provisioning-with-aws-service-catalog-connector-for-jira-service-desk/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:11:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:42:45+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e announces the AWS Service Catalog Connector for Jira Service Desk (JSD) version 1.0.4. With this connector, administrators can use existing AWS Service Catalog configurations, including curated products, portfolios, constraints, and tagging, and expose them to JSD administrators and users. This new connector simplifies AWS product provisioning and provides administrators with governance and oversight over their AWS resources.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing the Connector for Jira Service Desk, administrators can view AWS Service Catalog portfolios and products, align them to organizational structures, grant access to JSD users, and connect JSD workflows to provisioning requests. JSD end users can browse and request provisioning of AWS Service Catalog products, including AWS Marketplace software products that have been copied to AWS Service Catalog. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS-supplied connector is available at no charge in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/1221283/aws-service-catalog-connector-for-jsd?hosting\u003ddatacenter\u0026amp;tab\u003doverview\"\u003eAtlassian Marketplace\u003c/a\u003e. This new feature is generally available in all AWS Regions where AWS Service Catalog is available. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, open your Jira instance, choose Add-ons, then find and install the AWS Service Catalog Connector for Jira Service Desk. Learn more about AWS Service Catalog \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-11-22T20:00:29Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/simplify-cloud-provisioning-with-aws-service-catalog-connector-for-jira-service-desk/","postDateTime":"2019-11-22T12:34:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Simplify cloud provisioning with AWS Service Catalog Connector for Jira Service Desk","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/servicecatalog.html\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e announces the AWS Service Catalog Connector for Jira Service Desk (JSD) version 1.0.4. With this connector, administrators can use existing AWS Service Catalog configurations, including curated products, portfolios, constraints, and tagging, and expose them to JSD administrators and users. This new connector simplifies AWS product provisioning and provides administrators with governance and oversight over their AWS resources.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-11-new-aws-service-catalog-connector-for-servicenow-supports-budgets-integration-and-fips-endpoints","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/new-aws-service-catalog-connector-for-servicenow-supports-budgets-integration-and-fips-endpoints/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:34:50+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS announces a new Service Catalog Connector for ServiceNow (version 2.3.3). Administrators now have budget, actual, and forecast spend visibility within the connector. Using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2019/09/service-catalog-announces-budget-visibility/\"\u003eService Catalog Budgets Visibility\u003c/a\u003e, administrators can create and associate budgets with portfolios and products to track spend. The new ServiceNow connector also supports FIPS endpoints, enabling enterprises and government entities operating in GovCloud West to use the connector.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOther enhancements in this release include end-user control over StackSet instances, viewing of provisioned product events, and closure of the ServiceNow request items when provisioned products are terminated. The AWS-supplied connector is available in the ServiceNow Store for the London (L), Madrid (M), and New York (N) versions of ServiceNow. This feature is available in all commercial and GovCloud regions where AWS Service Catalog and AWS Budgets are available.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eService Catalog\u003c/a\u003e is used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and distribute approved applications on AWS. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/aws-cost-management/aws-budgets/\"\u003eAWS Budgets\u003c/a\u003e lets you set custom cost budgets that alert you when your costs exceed, or are forecasted to exceed, your budgeted amount. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLearn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog.\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-11-21T01:39:02Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/new-aws-service-catalog-connector-for-servicenow-supports-budgets-integration-and-fips-endpoints/","postDateTime":"2019-11-19T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"New AWS Service Catalog Connector for ServiceNow supports Budgets integration and FIPS endpoints","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS announces a new Service Catalog Connector for ServiceNow (version 2.3.3). Administrators now have budget, actual, and forecast spend visibility within the connector. Using \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/about-aws/whats-new/2019/09/service-catalog-announces-budget-visibility.html\"\u003eService Catalog Budgets Visibility\u003c/a\u003e, administrators can create and associate budgets with portfolios and products to track spend. The new ServiceNow connector also supports FIPS endpoints, enabling enterprises and government entities operating in GovCloud West to use the connector.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-10-aws-service-catalog-enables-transfer-of-provisioned-product-ownership","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/aws-service-catalog-enables-transfer-of-provisioned-product-ownership/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:15:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:29:21+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now enables administrators and team members to change the ownership of their provisioned products. With this feature, when team members or responsibilities change, ownership of their provisioned products can easily be transferred to a new team member or role.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs an administrator, you are now able to transfer provisioned product ownership within your organization. You are able to see the complete ownership history of every provisioned product, allowing you to monitor and audit resource ownership. When transferring ownership of provisioned products, you empower the new user or role to take operational action on the provisioned product with access to its complete history.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog is used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis new feature is generally available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eregions\u003c/a\u003e where AWS Service Catalog is available. To get started, administrators set up their IAM permissions for their use case. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about AWS Service Catalog operational capabilities, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/introduction.html\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog Administrator Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-31T21:04:51Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/aws-service-catalog-enables-transfer-of-provisioned-product-ownership/","postDateTime":"2019-10-31T12:31:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog enables transfer of provisioned product ownership","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog now enables administrators and team members to change the ownership of their provisioned products. With this feature, when team members or responsibilities change, ownership of their provisioned products can easily be transferred to a new team member or role.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#application-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"application-services","description":"marketing:marchitecture/application-services","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#security-identity-and-compliance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"security-identity-and-compliance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/security-identity-and-compliance","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#cost-management","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"cost-management","description":"marketing:marchitecture/cost-management","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:11+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-09-service-catalog-announces-budget-visibility","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/09/service-catalog-announces-budget-visibility/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:13:28+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now provides budget visibility on your portfolios and products by integrating with AWS Budgets. With this feature you can create and associate budgets with portfolios and products and track your spend. Portfolio and product budget creation is simplified using TagOptions and AutoTags, providing administrators with visibility into the budget and month-to-date spend. To get started, activate your tags and create your budget in AWS Budgets, then associate that budget to your portfolio or product in AWS Service Catalog. This feature is available in all commercial regions where AWS Service Catalog and AWS Budgets are available.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Budgets lets you set custom cost budgets that alert you when your costs exceed, or are forecasted to exceed, your budgeted amount.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog is used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Service Catalog budget visibility and administration, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/catalogs_budgets.html\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog Administrator Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:02:26Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/09/service-catalog-announces-budget-visibility/","postDateTime":"2019-09-12T04:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Announces Budget Visibility","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/servicecatalog.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now provides budget visibility on your portfolios and products by integrating with AWS Budgets. With this feature you can create and associate budgets with portfolios and products and track your spend. Portfolio and product budget creation is simplified using TagOptions and AutoTags, providing administrators with visibility into the budget and month-to-date spend. To get started, activate your tags and create your budget in AWS Budgets, then associate that budget to your portfolio or product in AWS Service Catalog. This feature is available in all commercial regions where AWS Service Catalog and AWS Budgets are available.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#cost-management","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"cost-management","description":"marketing:marchitecture/cost-management","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:11+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-audience#enterprises","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-audience","name":"enterprises","description":"marketing:audience/enterprises","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:08:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:08:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-budgets","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-budgets","description":"general:products/aws-budgets","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:55:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:55:47+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-05-service-catalog-servicenow-connector-now-supports-stacksets","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/service-catalog-servicenow-connector-now-supports-stacksets/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:11:52+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:20:39+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe new \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/?nc2\u003dh_m1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e Connector for ServiceNow supports AWS CloudFormation StackSets and ChangeSets. StackSets enables provisioning of AWS Service Catalog products across AWS accounts and regions from the ServiceNow platform. ChangeSets enables ServiceNow users to see the planned changes to their resources prior to provisioning or updating a Service Catalog provisioned product. AWS Service Catalog is used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and distribute approved applications on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Service Catalog Connector for ServiceNow allows you to expose your existing AWS Service Catalog configuration, including curated products, portfolios, constraints, and tagging, to your ServiceNow administrators and users. ServiceNow administrators can use the connector to view AWS Service Catalog portfolios and products, and enable ServiceNow users to self-service view and provision these products. The AWS-supplied connector is available in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://store.servicenow.com/sn_appstore_store.do#!/store/application/f0b117a3db32320093a7d7a0cf961912/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eServiceNow Store\u003c/a\u003e for the Kingston (K), London (L), and Madrid (M) versions of ServiceNow.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLearn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"http://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:52Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/service-catalog-servicenow-connector-now-supports-stacksets/","postDateTime":"2019-05-08T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Connector for ServiceNow supports CloudFormation StackSets","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe new \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/?nc2\u003dh_m1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e Connector for ServiceNow supports AWS CloudFormation StackSets and ChangeSets. StackSets enables provisioning of AWS Service Catalog products across AWS accounts and regions from the ServiceNow platform. ChangeSets enables ServiceNow users to see the planned changes to their resources prior to provisioning or updating a Service Catalog provisioned product. AWS Service Catalog is used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and distribute approved applications on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Service Catalog Connector for ServiceNow allows you to expose your existing AWS Service Catalog configuration, including curated products, portfolios, constraints, and tagging, to your ServiceNow administrators and users. ServiceNow administrators can use the connector to view AWS Service Catalog portfolios and products, and enable ServiceNow users to self-service view and provision these products. The AWS-supplied connector is available in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://store.servicenow.com/sn_appstore_store.do#!/store/application/f0b117a3db32320093a7d7a0cf961912/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eServiceNow Store\u003c/a\u003e for the Kingston (K), London (L), and Madrid (M) versions of ServiceNow.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLearn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"http://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-audience#government-and-education","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-audience","name":"government-and-education","description":"marketing:audience/government-and-education","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-audience#enterprises","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-audience","name":"enterprises","description":"marketing:audience/enterprises","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:08:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:08:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-audience#public-sector-government","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-audience","name":"public-sector-government","description":"marketing:audience/public-sector-government","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-03-aws-service-catalog-now-available-in-aws-govcloud-us-west-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/03/aws-service-catalog-now-available-in-aws-govcloud-us-west-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:03:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:16:06+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e in the AWS GovCloud (US-West) Region, an AWS Region designed to host sensitive data and regulated workloads in the cloud for customers who have U.S. federal, state, and local government compliance requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog allows you to centrally manage commonly deployed IT services, and helps you achieve consistent governance and meet your compliance requirements, while enabling users to quickly deploy only the approved IT services they need.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eLearn more about the AWS GovCloud (US)\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:34Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/03/aws-service-catalog-now-available-in-aws-govcloud-us-west-region/","postDateTime":"2019-03-20T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog is now available in the AWS GovCloud (US) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e in the AWS GovCloud (US-West) Region, an AWS Region designed to host sensitive data and regulated workloads in the cloud for customers who have U.S. federal, state, and local government compliance requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog allows you to centrally manage commonly deployed IT services, and helps you achieve consistent governance and meet your compliance requirements, while enabling users to quickly deploy only the approved IT services they need.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eLearn more about the AWS GovCloud (US)\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-01-aws-config-adds-support-for-aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/aws-config-adds-support-for-aws-service-catalog/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:08:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:07:42+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/config/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Config\u003c/a\u003e to record configuration changes to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, a service that allows customers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS. With AWS Config, you can track changes to the configuration of an AWS Service Catalog portfolio, such as addition or removal of launch constraints, tags and accounts with which the portfolio has been shared.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  You can also view the AWS Service Catalog products associated with a portfolio as well as the products provisioned from the portfolio. AWS Config maintains the configuration change history for these AWS Service Catalog resource types, which you can access through the AWS Config console or APIs. This data can be used for audit purposes as well as for operational troubleshooting. For example, you can use this data to understand how a certain AWS Service Catalog user changed a portfolio constraint and when that change occurred.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSupport for AWS Service Catalog in AWS Config is available in all AWS public Regions where AWS Service Catalog is offered. For the full list of supported Regions, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/rande.html#servicecatalog_region\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Regions and Endpoints\u003c/a\u003e in the AWS General Reference.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about AWS Config, see the following:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/config/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eProduct Page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/resource-config-reference.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSupported Resources\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/documentation/config/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDocumentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about AWS Service Catalog, see the following:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eProduct Page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/index.html?id\u003ddocs_gateway#lang/en_us\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDocumentation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:55Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/aws-config-adds-support-for-aws-service-catalog/","postDateTime":"2019-01-11T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Config adds support for AWS Service Catalog","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/config/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Config\u003c/a\u003e to record configuration changes to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, a service that allows customers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS. With AWS Config, you can track changes to the configuration of an AWS Service Catalog portfolio, such as addition or removal of launch constraints, tags and accounts with which the portfolio has been shared.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-config","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-config","description":"general:products/aws-config","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-12-aws-service-catalog-announces-integration-with-aws-organizations","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/12/aws-service-catalog-announces-integration-with-aws-organizations/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:59:15+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS Service Catalog, a service to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS, now integrates with AWS Organizations. With this feature, you can simplify sharing of AWS Service Catalog portfolios across member accounts in your organization. AWS Organizations offers policy-based management for multiple AWS accounts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Now, AWS Service Catalog administrators no longer need to have the receiving account ID or portfolio ID on hand. You can save time and reduce the risk of error with manually sharing portfolio and account IDs. Using your organization’s master account, you can share portfolios to member accounts by referencing an existing organizational unit or organization ID without leaving AWS Service Catalog. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClick to learn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/?nc2\u003dh_m1\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/organizations/\"\u003eAWS Organizations\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:17Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/12/aws-service-catalog-announces-integration-with-aws-organizations/","postDateTime":"2018-12-06T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Announces Integration with AWS Organizations","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS Service Catalog, a service to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS, now integrates with AWS Organizations. With this feature, you can simplify sharing of AWS Service Catalog portfolios across member accounts in your organization. AWS Organizations offers policy-based management for multiple AWS accounts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Now, AWS Service Catalog administrators no longer need to have the receiving account ID or portfolio ID on hand. You can save time and reduce the risk of error with manually sharing portfolio and account IDs. Using your organization’s master account, you can share portfolios to member accounts by referencing an existing organizational unit or organization ID without leaving AWS Service Catalog. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClick to learn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/?nc2\u003dh_m1\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/organizations/\"\u003eAWS Organizations\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-11-aws-service-catalog-connector-for-servicenow-supports-self-service-actions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/aws-service-catalog-connector-for-servicenow-supports-self-service-actions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:00:54+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS Service Catalog, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS, is announcing an update to AWS Service Catalog Connector for ServiceNow. The connector allows you to use your existing AWS Service Catalog configuration, including curated products, portfolios, constraints, and tagging, and expose this to your ServiceNow administrators and users.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  With the version 1.6.7 release, ServiceNow users can now request Self-Service Actions that have been configured in AWS Service Catalog. Self-Service Actions operate on AWS provisioned products, and allow users to perform governed operations on their AWS resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  The AWS-supplied connector is available in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://store.servicenow.com/sn_appstore_store.do#!/store/home\"\u003eServiceNow Store\u003c/a\u003e for Jakarta (J), Kingston (K), and London (L) versions of ServiceNow.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Click \u003ca href\u003d\"http://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about AWS Service Catalog.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:32Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/aws-service-catalog-connector-for-servicenow-supports-self-service-actions/","postDateTime":"2018-11-19T14:07:56Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Connector for ServiceNow v1.6.7 supports Self-Service Actions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS Service Catalog, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS, is announcing an update to AWS Service Catalog Connector for ServiceNow. The connector allows you to use your existing AWS Service Catalog configuration, including curated products, portfolios, constraints, and tagging, and expose this to your ServiceNow administrators and users.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general#products","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general","name":"products","description":"general:products","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:34+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-10-aws-service-catalog-announces-self-service-actions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/aws-service-catalog-announces-self-service-actions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:41:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:51:34+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS Service Catalog, used by enterprises to organize and govern cloud resources on AWS, now enables your end users to perform self-service actions on your provisioned products, without needing to grant end users full access to AWS services. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSelf-service actions are based on AWS Systems Manager automation documents, and you can discover allowed public actions in the Service Catalog Self-Service Action library. A library of pre-defined public actions is available- which include stop, start, and reboot for EC2 and RDS instances. You can also define custom, private actions. Your end users can invoke these actions without needing to contact your administrator.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  You can define an IAM role for invocation and associate actions with Service Catalog products and product versions. After association they become available to your users, as actions, on their provisioned products. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about AWS Service Catalog Self-Service Actions click \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/using-service-actions.html\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e and learn more about AWS Service Catalog click \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:06Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/aws-service-catalog-announces-self-service-actions/","postDateTime":"2018-10-17T11:02:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Announces Self-Service Actions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS Service Catalog, used by enterprises to organize and govern cloud resources on AWS, now enables your end users to perform self-service actions on your provisioned products, without needing to grant end users full access to AWS services. \u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-10-aws-service-catalog-connector-for-servicenow-announces-new-features","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/aws-service-catalog-connector-for-servicenow-announces-new-features/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:32:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:31:43+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS Service Catalog has announced new features to the AWS Service Catalog Connector for ServiceNow. The connector allows you to use your existing AWS Service Catalog configuration, including curated products, portfolios, constraints, and tagging, and expose this to your ServiceNow administrators and users.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  With the version 1.5.1 release, ServiceNow administrators can use the ServiceNow Portal View, configure the connector to use multiple AWS accounts, and validate account setup. ServiceNow users now have the ability to perform updates to provisioned products, which will create a closed change request record in ServiceNow’s Change Management application. There is also the ability for developers to call Service Catalog APIs from ServiceNow through the connector, enabling extensions to connector functionality. This simplifies AWS product provisioning for ServiceNow users and provides ServiceNow administrators governance and oversight over AWS products.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Service Catalog Connector for ServiceNow is available in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://store.servicenow.com/sn_appstore_store.do#!/store/home\"\u003eServiceNow Store\u003c/a\u003e for Jakarta (J), Kingston (K), and London (L) versions of ServiceNow.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  To learn more about AWS Service Catalog visit \u003ca href\u003d\"http://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:06Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/aws-service-catalog-connector-for-servicenow-announces-new-features/","postDateTime":"2018-10-17T10:55:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Connector for ServiceNow Announces New Features","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS Service Catalog has announced new features to the AWS Service Catalog Connector for ServiceNow. The connector allows you to use your existing AWS Service Catalog configuration, including curated products, portfolios, constraints, and tagging, and expose this to your ServiceNow administrators and users.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-10-aws-service-catalog-adds-integration-with-aws-codepipeline","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/aws-service-catalog-adds-integration-with-aws-codepipeline/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:27:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:55:49+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, a service to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS, now supports \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS CodePipeline\u003c/a\u003e. AWS CodePipeline is a fully managed continuous delivery (CD) service that helps you automate release pipelines for fast and reliable updates. Now you can use continuous delivery practices to publish and update product versions in AWS Service Catalog. You can configure a CodePipeline pipeline to automatically trigger based off an update to your code in AWS CodeCommit, Amazon S3, or GitHub.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProducts in AWS Service Catalog map to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudformation/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS CloudFormation\u003c/a\u003e templates, along with metadata, which provide control and governance at launch time. Previously, template authors had no easy, automated, and safe way to publish product or template updates in Service Catalog. Every update required authors to engage Service Catalog administrators within their organizations. Now, AWS CodePipeline can play the role of the Service Catalog administrator and run the necessary pre-approvals and tests before publishing an update to Service Catalog.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLearn more about using AWS CodePipeline with AWS Service Catalog by visiting our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/tutorials-S3-servicecatalog.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. This feature is available in all regions that CodePipeline and Service catalog are available. For a full list of AWS Regions where CodePipeline and Service catalog are available, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eregion table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:02Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/aws-service-catalog-adds-integration-with-aws-codepipeline/","postDateTime":"2018-10-16T15:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Adds Integration with AWS CodePipeline","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/servicecatalog.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, a service to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS, now supports \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/codepipeline.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS CodePipeline\u003c/a\u003e. AWS CodePipeline is a fully managed continuous delivery (CD) service that helps you automate release pipelines for fast and reliable updates. Now you can use continuous delivery practices to publish and update product versions in AWS Service Catalog. You can configure a CodePipeline pipeline to automatically trigger based off an update to your code in AWS CodeCommit, Amazon S3, or GitHub.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-codepipeline","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-codepipeline","description":"general:products/aws-codepipeline","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:04+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-10-resource-groups-tagging-api-supports-additional-aws-services","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/resource-groups-tagging-api-supports-additional-aws-services/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:23:57+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:59:57+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use the Resource Groups Tagging API to centrally manage tags and search resources for 6 additional AWS Services: Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, AWS Secrets Manager, AWS Certificate Manager Private CA, AWS IoT Analytics, Amazon Aurora, and AWS Service Catalog.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Resource Groups Tagging API is a single central point reaching across 47 AWS services to programmatically perform operations including tag resources, untag resources, list unique tag keys, list tag values, and search for resources with specific tags. To get started with and to view the list of supported AWS Services, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/resourcegroupstagging/latest/APIReference/Welcome.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eResource Groups Tagging API documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/resource-groups-tagging-api-supports-additional-aws-services/","postDateTime":"2018-10-11T11:08:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Resource Groups Tagging API Supports Additional AWS Services","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use the Resource Groups Tagging API to centrally manage tags and search resources for 6 additional AWS Services: Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, AWS Secrets Manager, AWS Certificate Manager Private CA, AWS IoT Analytics, Amazon Aurora, and AWS Service Catalog.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-secrets-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-secrets-manager","description":"general:products/aws-secrets-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:06+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-certificate-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-certificate-manager","description":"general:products/aws-certificate-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:02+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-tools-aws-resource-groups","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-tools-aws-resource-groups","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-tools/aws-resource-groups","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:01:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:01:31+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-aurora","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-aurora","description":"general:products/amazon-aurora","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-iot-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-iot-analytics","description":"general:products/aws-iot-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-07-aws-service-catalog-launches-support-for-cloudformation-change-sets","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/aws-service-catalog-launches-support-for-cloudformation-change-sets/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:39:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:51:41+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/?nc2\u003dh_m1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS, now supports CloudFormation Change Sets. This also includes CloudFormation Transforms, which provides capability for the Serverless Application Model (SAM). \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Change Sets allow you to launch and update application stacks with confidence by providing a preview of the changes that will be made to AWS resources before they are executed, and give visibility into whether proposed changes will add, delete, or replace any resources. AWS CloudFormation makes the changes to a stack only when you decide to execute the Change Set, allowing you to decide whether to proceed with the proposed changes immediately, at a later date, or to explore different changes by creating another change set. AWS Service Catalog supports CloudFormation Change Sets natively via API and console. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLearn more about AWS Service Catalog \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:17Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/aws-service-catalog-launches-support-for-cloudformation-change-sets/","postDateTime":"2018-07-25T22:01:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Launches Support for CloudFormation Change Sets","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/?nc2\u003dh_m1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS, now supports CloudFormation Change Sets. This also includes CloudFormation Transforms, which provides capability for the Serverless Application Model (SAM). \u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-07-aws-service-catalog-now-supports-service-catalog-resources-in-cloudformation","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/aws-service-catalog-now-supports-service-catalog-resources-in-cloudformation/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:38:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:54:07+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS, now supports the ability for you to use AWS CloudFormation to create Service Catalog resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  With this feature release, you can configure your desired Service Catalog environment in a reusable CloudFormation template. This helps you to simplify and standardize your Service Catalog setup across your enterprise environment. You can create CloudFormation templates to configure portfolios and products, associate users to portfolios, and associate TagOptions to portfolios and products. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  This new feature also enables you to create your own reusable administrative Service Catalog products to replicate your Service Catalog environments across regions and accounts, reducing manual work and human error, and eliminating the need for custom coding.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  To find the supported Service Catalog resources on using this feature with CloudFormation templates, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-template-resource-type-ref.html\"\u003eCloudFormation Resource Types Reference\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about AWS Service Catalog, click \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:23Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/aws-service-catalog-now-supports-service-catalog-resources-in-cloudformation/","postDateTime":"2018-07-13T13:34:13Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Now Supports Service Catalog Resources in CloudFormation","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS, now supports the ability for you to use AWS CloudFormation to create Service Catalog resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-06-introducing-aws-landing-zone","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/06/introducing-aws-landing-zone/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:38:33+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:52:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/answers/aws-landing-zone/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Landing Zone\u003c/a\u003e is a solution that helps customers more quickly set up a secure, multi-account AWS environment based on AWS best practices. With the large number of design choices, setting up a multi-account environment can take a significant amount of time, involve the configuration of multiple accounts and services, and require a deep understanding of AWS services. This solution can help save time by automating the set-up of an  environment for running secure and scalable workloads while implementing  an initial security baseline through the creation of core accounts and  resources. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Landing Zone deploys an AWS Account Vending Machine (AVM) product for provisioning and automatically configuring new accounts.\u0026nbsp;The AVM leverages \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/single-sign-on/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Single Sign-On\u003c/a\u003e for managing user account access. This environment is customizable to allow customers to implement their own account baselines through a Landing Zone configuration and update pipeline. To learn more about AWS Landing Zone, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/answers/aws-landing-zone/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003esolution webpage\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditional solution offerings can be found on the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/answers/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Answers webpage\u003c/a\u003e, where you can browse common questions by category. These pages provide a combination of Solution Briefs and comprehensive Solutions, which are AWS-vetted, automated, turnkey reference implementations that address specific business needs.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRegister for the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://pages.awscloud.com/Launch-AWS-Faster-using-Automated-Landing-Zones_0606-ENT.html?\u0026amp;trk\u003del_a131L000005ixrdQAA\u0026amp;trkCampaign\u003dJune_0606-ENT\u0026amp;sc_channel\u003del\u0026amp;sc_campaign\u003dpac_Q2-2018_exlinks_PMM_OTT_06DGAB\u0026amp;sc_outcome\u003dPaaS_Digital_Marketing\u0026amp;sc_geo\u003dNAMER\u0026amp;sc_country\u003dmult\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Landing Zone Webinar\u003c/a\u003e on June 19, 2018.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/06/introducing-aws-landing-zone/","postDateTime":"2018-06-14T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing AWS Landing Zone","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/answers/aws-landing-zone.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Landing Zone\u003c/a\u003e is a solution that helps customers more quickly set up a secure, multi-account AWS environment based on AWS best practices. With the large number of design choices, setting up a multi-account environment can take a significant amount of time, involve the configuration of multiple accounts and services, and require a deep understanding of AWS services. This solution can help save time by automating the set-up of an  environment for running secure and scalable workloads while implementing  an initial security baseline through the creation of core accounts and  resources. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general#products","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general","name":"products","description":"general:products","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:34+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-single-sign-on","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-single-sign-on","description":"general:products/aws-single-sign-on","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-05-aws-service-catalog-launches-ability-to-copy-products-across-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/aws-service-catalog-launches-ability-to-copy-products-across-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:25:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:54:45+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/?nc2\u003dh_m1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS, now allows administrators, via the console, to copy products across AWS Service Catalog supported \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS regions\u003c/a\u003e. This makes it easier for administrators to manage products across their enterprise.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo copy across AWS regions, administrators specify the product and version(s) they wish to copy, select the destination region, and the product will become available in the destination region’s product list to be assigned to portfolios. The copy function will copy product name, version(s), and TagOptions to the destination region. There is also an API for copying products. Learn more \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/dg/API_CopyProduct.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLearn more about AWS Service Catalog by visiting the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/?nc2\u003dh_m1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:30Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/aws-service-catalog-launches-ability-to-copy-products-across-regions/","postDateTime":"2018-05-03T16:02:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Launches Ability to Copy Products Across Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/?nc2\u003dh_m1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS, now allows administrators, via the console, to copy products across AWS Service Catalog supported \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS regions\u003c/a\u003e. This makes it easier for administrators to manage products across their enterprise.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-05-new-aws-service-catalog-connector-for-servicenow-simplifies-cloud-provisioning","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/new-aws-service-catalog-connector-for-servicenow-simplifies-cloud-provisioning/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:30:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:01:23+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/?nc2\u003dh_m1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS, is announcing the AWS Service Catalog Connector for ServiceNow. The connector allows you to use your existing AWS Service Catalog configuration, including curated products, portfolios, constraints, and tagging, and expose this to your ServiceNow administrators and users.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  ServiceNow administrators can view AWS Service Catalog portfolios and products, align them to organizational structures such as teams, grant access to ServiceNow users, and connect ServiceNow workflows to provisioning requests. ServiceNow users can browse and request provisioning of AWS Service Catalog products, which can include AWS Marketplace software products that have been copied to AWS Service Catalog. This simplifies AWS product provisioning for ServiceNow users and provides ServiceNow administrators governance and oversight over AWS products.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS-supplied connector is available in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://store.servicenow.com/sn_appstore_store.do#!/store/application/f0b117a3db32320093a7d7a0cf961912/1.0.3?referer\u003dsn_appstore_store.do%23!%2Fstore%2Fsearch%3Fq%3Daws\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eServiceNow Store\u003c/a\u003e for the Helsinki (H), Istanbul (I), Jakarta (J), and Kingston (K) versions of ServiceNow.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Learn more about AWS Service Catalog \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/?nc2\u003dh_m1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:30Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/new-aws-service-catalog-connector-for-servicenow-simplifies-cloud-provisioning/","postDateTime":"2018-05-02T11:07:55Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"New AWS Service Catalog Connector for ServiceNow Simplifies Cloud Provisioning","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/?nc2\u003dh_m1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS, is announcing the AWS Service Catalog Connector for ServiceNow. The connector allows you to use your existing AWS Service Catalog configuration, including curated products, portfolios, constraints, and tagging, and expose this to your ServiceNow administrators and users.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-05-aws-service-catalog-introduces-the-ability-to-chain-the-launch-of-multiple-products","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/aws-service-catalog-introduces-the-ability-to-chain-the-launch-of-multiple-products/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:22:21+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:44:05+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/?nc2\u003dh_m1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS, now allows customers to chain together the launch of multiple products. Customers gain the flexibility to compose products with smaller AWS CloudFormation templates as building blocks rather than creating a monolithic application stack template.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdministrators can chain together products during a launch. To do this, the initiating CloudFormation template will call the Service Catalog ProvisionProduct API as a CloudFormation resource, and reference the next product to launch. For example, administrators can create separate Amazon EC2 and Amazon RDS products and then have the completed EC2 product initiate the creation of the RDS product. This allows for independently maintained and versioned products and simple orchestration of a combined product launch.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLearn more about AWS Service Catalog by visiting the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/?nc2\u003dh_m1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  For details on adding this feature to a CloudFormation template, please see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-resource-servicecatalog-cloudformationprovisionedproduct.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eCloudFormationProvisionedProduct\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:31Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/aws-service-catalog-introduces-the-ability-to-chain-the-launch-of-multiple-products/","postDateTime":"2018-05-01T16:03:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Introduces the Ability to Chain the Launch of Multiple Products","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/?nc2\u003dh_m1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, and provision cloud resources on AWS, now allows customers to chain together the launch of multiple products. Customers gain the flexibility to compose products with smaller AWS CloudFormation templates as building blocks rather than creating a monolithic application stack template.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-03-aws-service-catalog-launches-brand-your-console-to-deliver-a-customizable-user-experience","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/03/aws-service-catalog-launches-brand-your-console-to-deliver-a-customizable-user-experience/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:29:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:41:26+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, provision, and operate cloud resources on AWS, now allows customers to customize the look and feel of the console. Customers can brand their AWS Service Catalog console to match their internal applications, making the user experience more seamless when moving from internal applications such as single sign-on and navigation portals to AWS Service Catalog. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog administrators can change the logo and color specifications to reflect their desired console branding. They have the flexibility to upload a logo in PNG, JPG, or SVG image file formats. Administrators can also choose a primary and accent color for other site components using a color picker or RGB color value. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLearn more about AWS Service Catalog by visiting the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e or go directly to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e to get started with Brand Your Console today.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:17Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/03/aws-service-catalog-launches-brand-your-console-to-deliver-a-customizable-user-experience/","postDateTime":"2018-03-08T15:22:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Launches Brand Your Console to Deliver a Customizable User Experience","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/servicecatalog.html\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to organize, govern, provision, and operate cloud resources on AWS, now allows customers to customize the look and feel of the console. Customers can brand their AWS Service Catalog console to match their internal applications, making the user experience more seamless when moving from internal applications such as single sign-on and navigation portals to AWS Service Catalog. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-03-aws-service-catalog-announces-autotags-for-automatic-tagging-of-provisioned-resources","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/03/aws-service-catalog-announces-autotags-for-automatic-tagging-of-provisioned-resources/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:29:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:03:49+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to create, govern, and manage a catalog of IT services, is announcing AutoTags. AutoTags are tags that identify the portfolio, product, and user that launched a product, and are automatically applied by AWS Service Catalog to provisioned resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the new AWS Service Catalog AutoTags, provisioned resources will be tagged with the unique identifiers for Portfolio, Product, and User. This provides a set of tags that reflect the AWS Service Catalog structure of portfolios, products, and users that customers have configured in the catalog. AutoTags do not count against the customer\u0027s 50-tag limit. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog AutoTags can help provide consistent tagging for your resources, which is useful when setting AWS Budgets for a portfolio, product, or user. You can also use the AutoTags to identify resources for post-launch operations such as setting AWS Config rules. AutoTags for your provisioned resources can be viewed in the Tags section of the downstream services used for provisioning, such as CloudFormation, EC2, and S3. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can take advantage of this new capability today by visiting AWS Service Catalog \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:15Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/03/aws-service-catalog-announces-autotags-for-automatic-tagging-of-provisioned-resources/","postDateTime":"2018-03-07T14:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Announces AutoTags for Automatic Tagging of Provisioned Resources","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/servicecatalog.html\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to create, govern, and manage a catalog of IT services, is announcing AutoTags. AutoTags are tags that identify the portfolio, product, and user that launched a product, and are automatically applied by AWS Service Catalog to provisioned resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-12-aws-service-catalog-announces-console-enhancements","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/12/aws-service-catalog-announces-console-enhancements/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:31:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:55:37+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to create, govern, and manage a catalog of IT services, is announcing enhancements to the Service Catalog console. These changes provide a simplified user experience to find and launch products in the catalog. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the new AWS Service Catalog console, products are shown as detailed cards with information such as product description, distributor, and owner. Product actions are readily accessible from the card. For example, AWS Service Catalog Administrators can take actions such as adding a product to a portfolio or deleting a product, and users can launch a product or update a provisioned product. All users also receive the ability to search across product metadata, and have simpler navigation that focuses on AWS Service Catalog products and actions. Users can choose between the product card or list view to find, launch, update, and terminate products more quickly. The console uses a responsive design to provide better usability across device types.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is available in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003e14 regions\u003c/a\u003e. You can take advantage of this new capability today by visiting AWS Service Catalog \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:55:05Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/12/aws-service-catalog-announces-console-enhancements/","postDateTime":"2017-12-14T15:15:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Announces Console Enhancements","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog, used by enterprises, system integrators, and managed service providers to create, govern, and manage a catalog of IT services, is announcing enhancements to the Service Catalog console. These changes provide a simplified user experience to find and launch products in the catalog. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-12-aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-14-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/12/aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-14-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:35:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:21:03+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is announcing that it is now available in new regions: Asia Pacific (Mumbai, Seoul), US West (N. California), and South America (Sao Paulo). With the latest release, AWS Service Catalog is now available in 14 regions including US East (N. Virginia, Ohio), US West (N. California, Oregon), Canada (Central), Europe (Ireland, Frankfurt, and London), South America (Sao Paulo) and Asia Pacific (Mumbai, Seoul, Singapore, Sydney, Tokyo).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog enables organizations on AWS to create, govern, and manage a catalog of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog allows you to centrally manage commonly deployed IT services, and helps you to achieve consistent governance and meet your compliance requirements, while enabling users to quickly deploy only the approved IT services that they need.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:55:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/12/aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-14-regions/","postDateTime":"2017-12-07T15:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog is now available in 14 regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is announcing that it is now available in new regions: Asia Pacific (Mumbai, Seoul), US West (N. California), and South America (Sao Paulo). With the latest release, AWS Service Catalog is now available in 14 regions including US East (N. Virginia, Ohio), US West (N. California, Oregon), Canada (Central), Europe (Ireland, Frankfurt, and London), South America (Sao Paulo) and Asia Pacific (Mumbai, Seoul, Singapore, Sydney, Tokyo).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-06-aws-service-catalog-tagoptions-library-creates-a-better-way-to-govern-your-aws-footprint","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/06/aws-service-catalog-tagoptions-library-creates-a-better-way-to-govern-your-aws-footprint/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:32:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:47:45+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog, the recommended tool for managing your approved software and infrastructure products on AWS, has announced a new feature called TagOptions Library to give customers, especially large enterprises, a better way to govern their AWS footprint.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTagOptions Library enables governance and standardization within AWS while maintaining agility for end-users. With this feature, Administrators perform a one-time copy of current tags to the new TagOptions Library, and can populate their TagOptions Library with hundreds of TagOptions that they govern, which can then be associated with portfolios and products. Administrator-defined TagOptions are either automatically applied to the product, at which point they become applied AWS tags. TagOptions on products cascade down as tags to each AWS resource being launched. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTagOptions Library paves the way for cost management, reporting and resource management.  Visit \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/tagoptions.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about the new AWS Service Catalog TagOptions Library.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:53:02Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/06/aws-service-catalog-tagoptions-library-creates-a-better-way-to-govern-your-aws-footprint/","postDateTime":"2017-06-28T13:45:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog TagOptions Library Creates a Better Way to Govern Your AWS Footprint","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog, the recommended tool for managing your approved software and infrastructure products on AWS, has announced a new feature called TagOptions Library to give customers, especially large enterprises, a better way to govern their AWS footprint.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-04-announcing-apn-service-delivery-program-for-aws-partners-with-service-catalog-expertise","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/04/announcing-apn-service-delivery-program-for-aws-partners-with-service-catalog-expertise/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:21:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:53:10+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Service Delivery Program helps AWS customers find qualified APN Partners that have demonstrated the ability to provide expertise in a specific service or skill area.  AWS Service Catalog partners help\u0026nbsp;create catalogs of IT services that are approved by the customer’s organization for use on AWS. With AWS\u0026nbsp;Service\u0026nbsp;Catalog, customers\u0026nbsp;and partners\u0026nbsp;can centrally manage commonly deployed IT services to help achieve consistent governance and meet compliance requirements\u0026nbsp;while enabling users to self-provision approved services.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe are launching with five initial AWS Service Catalog consulting partners.  Partners and customers can find more information about the program \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/partners/service-delivery/\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e, and view a list of partners \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/partners/\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:52:29Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/04/announcing-apn-service-delivery-program-for-aws-partners-with-service-catalog-expertise/","postDateTime":"2017-04-20T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing APN Service Delivery Program for AWS Partners with Service Catalog Expertise","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Service Delivery Program helps AWS customers find qualified APN Partners that have demonstrated the ability to provide expertise in a specific service or skill area.  AWS Service Catalog partners help\u0026nbsp;create catalogs of IT services that are approved by the customer’s organization for use on AWS. With AWS\u0026nbsp;Service\u0026nbsp;Catalog, customers\u0026nbsp;and partners\u0026nbsp;can centrally manage commonly deployed IT services to help achieve consistent governance and meet compliance requirements\u0026nbsp;while enabling users to self-provision approved services.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-02-aws-service-catalog-introduces-support-for-yaml-formatted-aws-cloudformation-templates","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/02/aws-service-catalog-introduces-support-for-yaml-formatted-aws-cloudformation-templates/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:31:52+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:45:03+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e                    You can now create Service Catalog Products using YAML-formatted AWS CloudFormation templates (YAML Version 1.1) in addition to JSON-formatted templates. This allows template creators to choose the format they feel most comfortable working in to describe AWS infrastructure. YAML-formatted CloudFormation templates follow the same anatomy as existing JSON-formatted templates.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can also view the CloudFormation documentation topic for YAML-formatted templates \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/template-formats.html\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. Visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/gettingstarted.templatebasics.html\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e for an introduction to CloudFormation template basics.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                    AWS Service Catalog is currently available in the US East (N. Virginia, Ohio), US West (Oregon), Canada (Central), Europe (Ireland, Frankfurt, and London) and Asia Pacific (Sydney, Singapore and Tokyo) Regions. For more information, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e product page.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:52:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/02/aws-service-catalog-introduces-support-for-yaml-formatted-aws-cloudformation-templates/","postDateTime":"2017-02-09T13:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Introduces Support for YAML-formatted AWS CloudFormation Templates","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e                    You can now create Service Catalog Products using YAML-formatted AWS CloudFormation templates (YAML Version 1.1) in addition to JSON-formatted templates. This allows template creators to choose the format they feel most comfortable working in to describe AWS infrastructure. YAML-formatted CloudFormation templates follow the same anatomy as existing JSON-formatted templates.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-01-aws-service-catalog-now-available-in-canada-and-london-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/01/aws-service-catalog-now-available-in-canada-and-london-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:30:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:43:25+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations on AWS to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS resources. These IT services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog allows you to centrally manage commonly deployed IT services, and helps you to achieve consistent governance and meet your compliance requirements, while enabling users to quickly deploy only the approved IT services that they need.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is currently available in the US East (N. Virginia, Ohio), US West (Oregon), Canada (Central), Europe (Ireland, Frankfurt, and London) and Asia Pacific (Sydney, Singapore and Tokyo) Regions. For more information, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e product page.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:51:52Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/01/aws-service-catalog-now-available-in-canada-and-london-regions/","postDateTime":"2017-01-05T14:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Now Available in Canada and London Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations on AWS to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS resources. These IT services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog allows you to centrally manage commonly deployed IT services, and helps you to achieve consistent governance and meet your compliance requirements, while enabling users to quickly deploy only the approved IT services that they need.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is currently available in the US East (N. Virginia, Ohio), US West (Oregon), Canada (Central), Europe (Ireland, Frankfurt, and London) and Asia Pacific (Sydney, Singapore and Tokyo) Regions. For more information, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/servicecatalog.html\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e product page.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-11-aws-service-catalog-administrator-api-set-now-available","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/11/aws-service-catalog-administrator-api-set-now-available/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:23:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:12:43+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, IT Administrators, IT Asset managers and Central Cloud teams can integrate with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e administrator actions using the AWS API and CLI. Previously, you could setup AWS Service Catalog products and portfolios only through the AWS Management Console. Now you can automate call patterns, or integrate with your private console or ITIL management tool. Additionally, we are announcing AWS Service Catalog APIs and admin console now support AWS CloudTrail logging. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                    The AWS Service Catalog and API are supported today in the following AWS Regions: US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), EU (Ireland), EU (Frankfurt), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Singapore), and Asia Pacific (Tokyo). To learn more see \u003ca href\u003d\"http://aws.amazon.com/documentation/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog documentation\u003c/a\u003e. You can also download the latest \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/tools/\"\u003eAWS SDK or CLI\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:51:12Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/11/aws-service-catalog-administrator-api-set-now-available/","postDateTime":"2016-11-17T09:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog Administrator API set now available","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, IT Administrators, IT Asset managers and Central Cloud teams can integrate with \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/servicecatalog.html\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e administrator actions using the AWS API and CLI. Previously, you could setup AWS Service Catalog products and portfolios only through the AWS Management Console. Now you can automate call patterns, or integrate with your private console or ITIL management tool. Additionally, we are announcing AWS Service Catalog APIs and admin console now support AWS CloudTrail logging. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-10-aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-the-europe-frankfurt-and-asia-pacific-sydney-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/10/aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-the-europe-frankfurt-and-asia-pacific-sydney-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:19:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:34:10+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog allows you to centrally manage commonly deployed IT services, and helps you achieve consistent governance and meet your compliance requirements, while enabling users to quickly deploy only the approved IT services they need.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is currently available in the US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), EU (Dublin and Frankfurt) and Asia Pacific (Sydney, Singapore and Tokyo) regions. For more information, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003ewebpage\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:50:59Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/10/aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-the-europe-frankfurt-and-asia-pacific-sydney-regions/","postDateTime":"2016-10-13T14:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog is now available in the Europe (Frankfurt) and Asia Pacific (Sydney) regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog allows you to centrally manage commonly deployed IT services, and helps you achieve consistent governance and meet your compliance requirements, while enabling users to quickly deploy only the approved IT services they need.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-09-aws-service-catalog-updated-access-policies-now-available","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/09/aws-service-catalog-updated-access-policies-now-available/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:26:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:37:20+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e                    Starting today, you can set access-level policies on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e post-launch actions. Previously, users would have access either to any provisioned product in the account or only to those which they themselves launched. Now, you can customize the access level for each action, with support for user, role, and account levels. This feature allows users to be granted access to view, update, terminate, and manage provisioned products created under their role or the account to which they are logged in. For more information about policies for these actions, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/documentation/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog documentation\u003c/a\u003e including the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/permissions.html#permissions-examples\"\u003eexample policies\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                  AWS Service Catalog is supported in the following AWS Regions: US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), EU (Ireland), Asia Pacific (Singapore), and Asia Pacific (Tokyo). You can also download the latest \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/tools/\"\u003eAWS SDK or CLI\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:50:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/09/aws-service-catalog-updated-access-policies-now-available/","postDateTime":"2016-09-15T14:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog updated access policies now available","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e                    Starting today, you can set access-level policies on \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/servicecatalog.html\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e post-launch actions. Previously, users would have access either to any provisioned product in the account or only to those which they themselves launched. Now, you can customize the access level for each action, with support for user, role, and account levels. This feature allows users to be granted access to view, update, terminate, and manage provisioned products created under their role or the account to which they are logged in. For more information about policies for these actions, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/documentation/servicecatalog.html\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog documentation\u003c/a\u003e including the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/permissions.html#permissions-examples\"\u003eexample policies\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-07-aws-service-catalog-user-api-set-now-available-and-product-version-limit-increased","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/07/aws-service-catalog-user-api-set-now-available-and-product-version-limit-increased/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:15:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:42:43+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, you can integrate with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e user actions using the API and CLI. Previously, you could integrate with AWS Service Catalog only through the AWS Management Console. Now you can automate call patterns or integrate with your private console. The AWS Service Catalog API and console now support AWS CloudTrail logging.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition, we are pleased to announce that the default limit for product versions has been raised to 50 product versions per product.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Service Catalog and User API are supported today in the following AWS Regions: US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), EU (Ireland), Asia Pacific (Singapore), and Asia Pacific (Tokyo). To learn more see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/documentation/servicecatalog/\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog documentation\u003c/a\u003e. You can also download the latest \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/tools/\"\u003eAWS SDK or CLI\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:50:34Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/07/aws-service-catalog-user-api-set-now-available-and-product-version-limit-increased/","postDateTime":"2016-07-08T09:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog User API Set now available and product version limit increased","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, you can integrate with \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/servicecatalog.html\"\u003eAWS Service Catalog\u003c/a\u003e user actions using the API and CLI. Previously, you could integrate with AWS Service Catalog only through the AWS Management Console. Now you can automate call patterns or integrate with your private console. The AWS Service Catalog API and console now support AWS CloudTrail logging.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2015-12-aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-the-asia-pacific-singapore-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/12/aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-the-asia-pacific-singapore-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:34:49+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs  of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT services can  include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and  databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service  Catalog allows you to centrally manage commonly deployed IT services,  and helps you achieve consistent governance and meet your compliance  requirements, while enabling users to quickly deploy only the approved  IT services they need.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is currently available in the US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), EU (Ireland), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), and Asia Pacific (Singapore) region. For more information, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003ewebpage\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:49:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/12/aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-the-asia-pacific-singapore-region/","postDateTime":"2015-12-16T12:53:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog is now available in the Asia Pacific (Singapore) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs  of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT services can  include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and  databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service  Catalog allows you to centrally manage commonly deployed IT services,  and helps you achieve consistent governance and meet your compliance  requirements, while enabling users to quickly deploy only the approved  IT services they need.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2015","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2015","description":"year#2015","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2015-12-aws-service-catalog-now-available-in-the-asia-pacific-tokyo-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/12/aws-service-catalog-now-available-in-the-asia-pacific-tokyo-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:29:10+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:40:06+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog allows you to centrally manage commonly deployed IT services, and helps you achieve consistent governance and meet your compliance requirements, while enabling users to quickly deploy only the approved IT services they need.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog is currently available in the US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), EU (Ireland) and Asia Pacific (Tokyo) regions. For more information, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003ewebpage\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:49:52Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/12/aws-service-catalog-now-available-in-the-asia-pacific-tokyo-region/","postDateTime":"2015-12-08T09:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog is now available in the Asia Pacific (Tokyo) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases to complete multi-tier application architectures. AWS Service Catalog allows you to centrally manage commonly deployed IT services, and helps you achieve consistent governance and meet your compliance requirements, while enabling users to quickly deploy only the approved IT services they need.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2015","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2015","description":"year#2015","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2015-10-aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-the-eu-west-ireland-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/10/aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-the-eu-west-ireland-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:38:25+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage  catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT  services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers,  software, and databases to complete multi-tier application  architectures. AWS Service Catalog allows you to centrally manage  commonly deployed IT services, and helps you achieve consistent  governance and meet your compliance requirements, while enabling users  to quickly deploy only the approved IT services they need.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  AWS Service Catalog is currently available in the US East (N.  Virginia), US West (Oregon) and EU (Ireland) regions. For more  information, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003ewebpage\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:49:43Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/10/aws-service-catalog-is-now-available-in-the-eu-west-ireland-region/","postDateTime":"2015-10-15T15:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Service Catalog is now available in the EU West (Ireland) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage  catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT  services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers,  software, and databases to complete multi-tier application  architectures. AWS Service Catalog allows you to centrally manage  commonly deployed IT services, and helps you achieve consistent  governance and meet your compliance requirements, while enabling users  to quickly deploy only the approved IT services they need.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  AWS Service Catalog is currently available in the US East (N.  Virginia), US West (Oregon) and EU (Ireland) regions. For more  information, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/servicecatalog.html\"\u003ewebpage\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2015","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2015","description":"year#2015","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2015-07-amazon-web-services-launches-aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/07/amazon-web-services-launches-aws-service-catalog/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:25:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:37:11+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage  catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT  services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers,  software, and databases to complete multi-tier application  architectures. AWS Service Catalog allows you to centrally manage  commonly deployed IT services, and helps you achieve consistent  governance and meet your compliance requirements, while enabling users  to quickly deploy only the approved IT services they need. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  To learn more about AWS Service Catalog, visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:49:30Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/07/amazon-web-services-launches-aws-service-catalog/","postDateTime":"2015-07-09T10:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Web Services launches AWS Service Catalog ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Service Catalog allows organizations to create and manage  catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. These IT  services can include everything from virtual machine images, servers,  software, and databases to complete multi-tier application  architectures. AWS Service Catalog allows you to centrally manage  commonly deployed IT services, and helps you achieve consistent  governance and meet your compliance requirements, while enabling users  to quickly deploy only the approved IT services they need. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  To learn more about AWS Service Catalog, visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/servicecatalog.html\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-service-catalog","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-service-catalog","description":"general:products/aws-service-catalog","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2015","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2015","description":"year#2015","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000"}]}],"metadata":{"count":93,"totalHits":93},"fieldTypes":{"regionalAvailability":"LongText","nofollow":"Boolean","date":"Date","language":"Text","title":"Text","postDateTime":"DateTime","body":"Text","postSummary":"LongText","ctaLabel":"Text","mediaThumbnail":"Text","nosnippet":"Boolean","price":"Text","ctaLink":"URL","headline":"Text","contentType":"Text","bodyBack":"LongText","secondaryCTALabel":"Text","primaryCTALink":"URL","noindex":"Boolean","level":"Text","heading":"Text","mediaType":"Text","mediaAlt":"Text","headlineUrl":"Text","mediaSrc":"URL","durationMinutes":"Number","badge":"JSON","videoImageUrl":"URL","postBody":"LongText","secondaryCTALink":"URL","Video":"URL","modifiedDate":"DateTime","namePerson":"Text","location":"Text","time":"Text","publishedDate":"DateTime","durationReadtime":"Number","primaryCTALabel":"Text"}}